\par\par \b \uc2 UK MARKET TALK ROUNDUP: BROKERS COMMENTS\b0\par\par\uc2 2,274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2010\par 16:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Broker comments in the UK today. Compiled by Dow Jones Newswires Markets Desk, markets.eu@dowjones.com \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1547 GMT [Dow Jones] Prudential's (PRU.LN) decision to stop selling insurance policies in Japan "is a relatively sensible move", noting Japan has a very competitive insurance market and Prudential has been "struggling to gain traction" in the country, says Panmure Gordon analyst Barrie Cornes. Says expects the Japanese business to have contributed only less than 2% of new business sales in 2009, making it "not particularly significant in terms of the overall picture of Prudential." Keeps buy rating and 732p target price. Shares -1.4% at 612p. (VDG)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1120 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  raises \uc2 Barratt Developments\uc2  (BDEV.LN) target price to 175p from 165p. "The positive margin and net debt trends improve the risk-reward profile of the company in our view, especially considering its depressed valuation relative to its peers," says brokerage. Adds the increased number of plots [of land] at full (or above average) gross margin is expected to drive a margin improvement over the next three years, "although our cautious outlook for UK house prices will limit the potential for normalized gross margins by 2013." Keeps buy rating. Shares -1% at 136p. (ISD)\par \par \uc2 1048 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 UBS\uc2  cuts \uc2 Trinity Mirror\uc2  (TNI.LN) to neutral from buy and decreases the price target to 185p from 220p. \uc2 UBS\uc2  thinks the stock's strong performance in '09 is unlikely to continue. \uc2 UBS\uc2  says given that investors are taking risk off the table and turn to solid, structural growth stories in the sector, Trinity is unlikely to fit the bill. However, the bank still thinks that a narrowing of the pension deficit through '10 should be supportive of the shares. Equally, Trinity is well placed to benefit from consolidation in the regionals space. Shares +2.5% at 173.1p. (ANT)\par \par \uc2 0946 GMT [Dow Jones] Pearson (PSON.LN) isn't expected to raise its 61% stake in \uc2 Interactive Data Corp\uc2  (IDC), says Citi. Pearson has announced that IDC's board is currently undertaking a preliminary review of strategic alternatives. "We would expect investor focus to be on the potential for a disposal, we would attach low probability to Pearson increasing its holding," says Citi. "The difficulty is knowing the tax base; although, because the business has been built largely organically and because Pearson has limited historical capital losses, there would be some tax leakage." Buy rating and 960p target. Shares +1.6% at 903p. (LEV)\par \par \uc2 0931 GMT [Dow Jones] Exane \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  adjusts ratings for mining stocks. Says improving macro data and flows back into equities should help stocks grind higher. Ups Antofagasta (ANTO.LN) to outperform from underperform and \uc2 Xstrata\uc2  (XTA.LN) to outperform from neutral; lifts targets to 1200p from 670p, and 1500p from 700p respectively. Has these as tactical bets, mainly on valuation grounds. Ups \uc2 Anglo American\uc2  (AAL.LN) to neutral from underperform, lifts target to 2600p from 1600p. Says the valuation leaves limited upside but management is pressured to deliver. Downgrades Vale (VALE) to underperform from neutral, lifts target to $29 from $23. Says it has one of the strongest growth pipelines but this is reflected fully in the valuation. (ANT)\par \par \uc2 0925 GMT [Dow Jones] Evolution Securities lifts \uc2 Imagination Technologies\uc2  (IMG.LN) target to 280p from 250p following a strong set of results from market leader Intel (INTC). The brokerage says full-year results will weigh on the success of Intel's 'Atom' chip for netbooks, which features Imagination's graphics technology, adding it could have a strong finish to the financial year as Intel's fourth quarter shipments feature in royalties. Adds Imagination is "in the sweetest of sweet spots," with booming end markets; and mass market adoption of mobile graphics technology each accelerating earnings growth. Shares flat at 250p. (ETB)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0902 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Interactive Data Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  (IDC) of which Pearson (PSON.LN) holds 61%, is expected to be sold, says Charles Stanley analyst Sam Hart. This comes after Pearson announced that IDC's board is "currently undertaking a preliminary review of strategic alternatives for the company." Hart cites the most likely buyers as Bloomberg, \f28 \uc2 \f2 McGraw-Hill\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Thomson Reuters. Hart would expect Pearson to use proceeds to strengthen its education business, which accounts for 60% of total earnings and sales. Accumulate rating on Pearson. Shares +2.1% at 906p. (LEV)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0901 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY's breach of 91.25 support suggests a completion of the corrective rebound from 84.84 to 93.21 says MIG bank's Howard Friend. He now sees risk toward the December 9th low of 87.35 and then the November low of 84.84. To negate this bearish outlook Friend says the spot would need to break back above 92.66. USD/JPY trades at 90.82. (GST)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0856 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  had warned that the time was not right to go long USD/JPY until the spot returned well above 92.00. It now trades at a 3-week low of 90.65 but the bank warns that rising risk appetite and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan ministry of finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official Kan favoring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , may make JPY gains short-lived again. The spot now trades at 90.76. (GST)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0855 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR higher late, last 9,205 vs 9,160 late Thursday; on USD's gains vs euro, regionals, short-covering ahead of weekend; "the spot opened higher and just hovered there the whole day," says dealer at foreign bank, adds, pair to stay in range next week; "there's not much domestic news this week and next so USD/IDR will be tracking external factors, especially movements in the euro and other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ." Dealers tip 9,170-9,220 range Monday. (RLC)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0854 GMT [Dow Jones] China onshore IRS down on profit taking, also on lower U.S. interest rates following weak retail sales, jobless claims data. 1-year down 3 bps at 2.24%-2.30%, 5-year down 7 bps at 3.85%-3.94%, 1-to-5-year spread 4 bps narrower at 163 bps. Swaps rose by more than 20 bps in past 2 weeks this year. "But downside in swaps is limited as inflation concerns are lingering and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is still likely to raise the yield in 1-year PBOC bills which will be auctioned Tuesday," says Shanghai-based foreign bank trader. (WYL)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0853 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR implied volatilities weak as early session momentum in spot pair loses steam, says foreign bank trader; 1-month ATMF at 8.20%/9.20% vs around 8.50%/9.50% late Thursday, but 1-year ATMF quoting at 8.75%/9.75%. "It's the same story. Volatility will continue to be offered, and the bias should remain downwards, particularly on the back-end. We could just see an inverted curve again at this rate, or at least a flat curve," says trader. Adds, $15 million 1-week ATMF seen dealt at 7.90% in early trade. Notes, 1-week vols held up as traders wary of being short gamma if spot moves up. (BIJ)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0852 GMT [Dow Jones] The cross plays are in the driving seat Friday with EUR/GBP and EUR/JPY selling weighing on EUR/USD and USD/JPY but supporting GBP/USD. EUR/CHF has an offered tone which is preventing USD/CHF from advancing. EUR/GBP printed a fresh 4-month low of 0.8812 earlier in the day, EUR/JPY a 3-week low of 130.48. (GST)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0851 GMT [Dow Jones] Risk appetite may be slumping at the moment but earnings reports from \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  later in Friday could start to turn things around. \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  reckons that there could even be a return to the 'perverse' negative correlation between the USD and US stocks that would help the carry trade. But, the bank says, there could be some book- squaring before the long weekend in the US first. (NEH)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0841 GMT [Dow Jones] Recent Swedish data may trigger some anxiety among Riksbank members, due to hold their next rate-setting meeting Feb. 10, says Handelsbanken. Says production has disappointed, and may weigh on GDP growth in 4Q. "However, inflation was substantially higher than expected in December, and high core inflation combined with a surge in inflation expectations and rapid credit growth could induce some anxiety among Riksbank members," it says. The board has been unanimous in recent decisions to hold the key rate at 0.25% but split on when rate increases should begin later this year. Sweden's two-year bond yields trade two basis points lower at 1.62% while the ten-year yield is two basis points lower at 3.38%. (ANM)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0839 GMT [Dow Jones] iTraxx Japan Series 12 rises slightly to 123 bps vs Thursday's 122, 121 bps as stronger JPY rekindles concerns over export-driven economy, boosting demand for protection against risks of credit default, says trader at Tokyo securities house. But adds Tokyo shares remain on upward trend, which could prompt investors to sell CDS, push iTraxx lower next week. Among single-name CDS deals on Friday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsui Fudosan Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (8801.TO) at 72 bps vs 80 bps on Dec. 22; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nippon Steel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (5401.TO) at 47 bps vs 55 bps on Dec. 8; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (8058.TO) at 48 bps vs 65 bps on Nov. 27; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsui & Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (8031.TO) at 60 bps vs 60, 55 bps on Jan. 8; Japan's sovereign CDS USD-denominated at 76 bps vs 74.5 bps on Wednesday. (TTA)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0838 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts open higher Friday as investors continue to worry about Greece and other peripherals. Another quiet UK data day awaits, and the theme is likely to continue to circulate around euro zone sovereign risks. Euro zone CPI and trade balance are due at 1000 GMT while US CPI and NY Fed Empire State survey are due 1330 GMT, industrial production at 1415 GMT and University Of Michigan confidence data at 1500 GMT. Gilt yield curve flattens: 2-year/10-year benchmark spread tightens to +276.0 bps from Thursday's +278.7 bps. March gilt futures up 0.29 at 115.06. 10-year benchmark gilt up 0.28 on at 104.209, yielding 3.946%. (NKA)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0834 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY slides to a fresh 3-week low of 90.65 with EUR/JPY sales weighing. Next support for the spot comes in at 90.35 says Mizuho's Nicole Elliott who adds that a weekly close below 91.00 should turn momentum bearish. (GST) [ 15-01-10 1547GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0902 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Interactive Data Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  (IDC) of which Pearson (PSON.LN) holds 61%, is expected to be sold, says Charles Stanley analyst Sam Hart. This comes after Pearson announced that IDC's board is "currently undertaking a preliminary review of strategic alternatives for the company." Hart cites the most likely buyers as Bloomberg, \f28 \uc2 \f2 McGraw-Hill\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Thomson Reuters. Hart would expect Pearson to use proceeds to strengthen its education business, which accounts for 60% of total earnings and sales. Accumulate rating on Pearson. Shares +2.1% at 906p. (LEV)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0847 GMT [Dow Jones] Man Group's (EMG.LN) AHL trading program performance has been "frustratingly poor" but \f28 \uc2 \f2 KBC Peel Hunt\f28 \uc2 \f2  doesn't think the strategy is broken and that short-term losses should give way to longer-term gains. "We believe that its strong long term track record together with the liquid and transparent nature will continue to attract inflows," KBC says, seeing inflows helping to offset the decline Man Group reported in 3Q assets under management. KBC keeps a buy rating and 403p price target. Shares down 3.9% at 302p. (MCP)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0759 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Balfour Beatty\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (BBY.LN) FY update shows that the group remains resilient says a trader. The trader says that trading is in-line and the order book looks quite healthy at GBP13.7B and notes also that average net cash increases to in excess of GBP300M for the second half of the year. The trader adds that the acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Parsons Brinckerhoff\f28 \uc2 \f2  enhances the group's offering. Shares closed Thursday at 282p. (ANT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0759 GMT [Dow Jones] Man Group's (EMH.LN) fiscal 3Q decline in assets is likely to disappoint the market, Cazenove says, "after the optimism that the company had been showing with respect to industry flows, which many had assumed would also benefit Man." Cazenove says it may adjust its fiscal 2010 earnings estimates slightly down and that consensus estimates for fiscal 2011 are now looking vulnerable. Cazenove keeps inline rating. Shares closed Thursday at 314p. (MCP)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0759 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bovis Homes\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' (BVS.LN) trading statement is in line with other sector peers' statements says Shore Capital. Shore says the de-stocking in the period and fund raising leave Bovis with a strong balance sheet. Shore remains cautious on the medium term outlook for the sector, given the prospects of rising unemployment, continued restrictions in the mortgage market and the prospects of further house price falls. But the brokerage thinks the company's strong balance sheet will provide some protection in the face of potential industry headwinds. Hold rating. Shares closed Thursday at 454.1p. (ANT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9288 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 15-01-10 1547GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1113   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100115e61f0016j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
