\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro falls vs dlr on ECB's Stark; U.S. data eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2010\par 02:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Euro falls vs dlr as Stark says Greece won't be bailed out\par \par \uc2 * Yen lower; eyes on policy implications if Fujii resigns\par \par \uc2 * Focus firmly on Friday's U.S. jobs data\par \par \uc2 By Jessica Mortimer\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 6 (Reuters) - The euro fell against the dollar on Wednesday after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  executive board member Juergen Stark was quoted in a media report as saying that the European Union would not bail out Greece.\par \par \uc2 The yen also weakened as Japanese investors picked up overseas assets at the start of the new year, while markets focused on possible successors to finance minister, Hirohisa Fujii, who may be forced out of office due to ill health.\par \par \uc2 Trading remained cautious ahead of key U.S. jobs data on Friday, however, as investors waited for evidence of how well the U.S. economy is faring.\par \par \uc2 The payroll data is expected to shape expectations for when the Federal Reserve will start tightening its ultra-loose monetary policy and determine the direction of the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "I think we'll go into the payrolls data roughly around these levels. After that we could see some big moves. Until then the euro could come under pressure on concerns about Greece," said Antje Praefcke, \uc2 Commerzbank\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist in Frankfurt.\par \par \uc2 The ECB's Stark said markets were "deluding themselves" in thinking member states would "put their hands in their wallets to save Greece", which renewed concerns about the fiscal health of some countries on the euro zone's periphery [ID:nLDE60504L]\par \par \uc2 At 0840 GMT, the euro <EUR=> was down 0.2 percent at $1.4335, though it was off a low of around $1.4285 reached shortly after the Stark comments, with some traders citing euro buying by sovereign names.\par \par \uc2 The euro showed little reaction to a purchasing managers' survey showing the euro zone's services sector expanded at its fastest pace in more than two years in December. [ID:nLAG006037]\par \par \uc2 The dollar index <DXY> rose 0.2 percent to 77.744 while the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained 0.4 percent against the yen <JPY=> to 92.09 yen, rebounding higher from Tuesday's low of 91.25 yen on trading platform EBS.\par \par \uc2 "Market players do not have a clear idea how \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will react after the U.S. jobs report on Friday, and they want to hedge against both upside and downside risks for the dollar," said a trader at a Japanese trust bank in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 Also in focus were the ADP's employment report and the ISM non-manufacturing index for December, along with the minutes from the Fed's last policy meeting, all due later in the day. <ECONUS>\par \par \uc2 FUJII AND HIS SUCCESSOR\par \par \uc2 Yen investors were concerned about possible changes to the Japanese government's fiscal stance and its policies to fight deflation if finance minister Fujii steps down. [ID:nT79774]\par \par \uc2 Some analysts said if Fujii were to resign, the yen could come under pressure, as some of his previous comments had given the impression that he accepted a strong Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Fujii's departure could mean a weaker yen because there is no one who has similar strong opinions about an appreciating yen expected to replace him," said Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  for \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "That could mean talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will return."\par \par \uc2 The euro rose 0.2 percent against the yen <EURJPY=R> to 132.06 yen.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Satomi Noguchi in Tokyo)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|J|NAT|UKI|RBN|ABN|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100106e6160001n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
