\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Recent quotes by policymakers on BOJ, economy\b0\par\par\uc2 842 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2009\par 23:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (For more stories on the Japanese economy, click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 18 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan may debate on Friday what options it has to loosen monetary policy early next year in the face of pressure from a government worried about the economy slipping back into recession as deflation erodes demand.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can afford to hold off on new policy initiatives this week having relieved some government pressure by putting in place a new funding \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  at an emergency meeting just two weeks ago. It is seen almost certain to leave its policy rate at just 0.1 percent on Friday.\par \par \uc2 A sudden spike in the yen or a tumble in Tokyo stocks deep enough to severely damage sentiment could prompt the BOJ to ease monetary policy further on Friday, although the chance of this happening is regarded as very small. [ID:nT74913]\par \par \uc2 Following are recent key quotes by BOJ and Japanese government officials on monetary policy and the economy:\par \par \uc2 BANKING MINISTER SHIZUKA KAMEI, DEC 16, in an interview:\par \par \uc2 "Japan's economy is now in a severe situation. Monetary easing is important but we also need fiscal stimulus to boost domestic demand. We need to have both in order for Japan to overcome deflation."\par \par \uc2 BOJ GOVERNOR MASAAKI SHIRAKAWA, Dec 2, to reporters after meeting Prime Minister Yukio Hatoyama:\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ and the government have the same view about deflation ... There was no request (from the government for further easing)."\par \par \uc2 BOJ BOARD MEMBER MIYAKO SUDA, Dec 2, in speech to business leaders in Kofu, central Japan:\par \par \uc2 "The costs and benefits (of any policy options) can change depending on the situation in financial markets. We are always open as to what will be the best policy measures.\par \par \uc2 "We need to remain cautious about suspicions on fiscal discipline boosting long-term bond yields. Monetisation of public debt by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can strengthen doubts about fiscal discipline."\par \par \uc2 KAMEI, Dec 2, to reporters:\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ was sleeping. It woke up a little bit and is still sleepy-headed."\par \par \uc2 SHIRAKAWA, Dec 1, at news conference after emergency policy board meeting:\par \par \uc2 "We judged that helping to lower term interest rates would be most effective in helping the economy recover ...\par \par \uc2 "We can say this (new \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pump three-month funds into the banking system at the overnight call rate of 0.1 percent) is quantitative easing in the broad sense that we are trying to ensure banks are not faced with (liquidity) constraints.\par \par \uc2 "I have no intention of monetising government debt nor do I think that this measure will lead to debt monetisation ...\par \par \uc2 "Since late last week there have been several moves in international finance, and the yen has risen and stock prices have dropped. Those moves were feared to negatively affect business sentiment and therefore the economy ...\par \par \uc2 "The government and the BOJ share the same understanding about the current situation. The BOJ was led to seek ways to make its easy monetary policy more effective."\par \par \uc2 SHIRAKAWA, Nov 30, in meeting with business leaders in Nagoya, central \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 "The government, not the BOJ, decides whether to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets ... The BOJ will closely examine how \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate volatility could affect the economy.\par \par \uc2 "We will patiently maintain an easy monetary policy, and I expect this to have some effect on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates ...\par \par \uc2 "The government recently expressed its view that the Japanese economy was in a mild deflationary phase in that the decline in prices was continuing. The BOJ's judgment on prices presented at the end of October is based on the same recognition ...\par \par \uc2 "The Bank will do its utmost to overcome deflation both in terms of monetary easing and ensuring the stability of the financial markets."\par \par \uc2 NATIONAL STRATEGY MINISTER NAOTO KAN, Nov 17, at news conference:\par \par \uc2 "We may have fallen into deflation ... I'm not speaking subjectively but based on objective data, and I believe the BOJ understands what backs up such a view ...\par \par \uc2 "I want to get on with exchanging opinions with the BOJ without infringing on its independence."\par \par \uc2 KAMEI, Nov 13, at news conference:\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ must be able to see underlying economic conditions.\par \par \uc2 "It must have the ability to look at what is behind statistics -- but it seems a bit weak at that."\par \par \uc2 SHIRAKAWA, Nov 7, at news conference after meeting of G20 finance ministers and central bankers in Scotland:\par \par \uc2 "I explained that the Bank of Japan will maintain very accommodative monetary conditions in guiding policy and steadily help the economy return to a sustainable growth path with price stability."\par \par \uc2 BOJ DEPUTY GOVERNOR HIROHIDE YAMAGUCHI, Nov 6, in parliament:\par \par \uc2 "The economy continues to recover modestly, and the chances of it experiencing a double dip are small."\par \par \uc2 KAN, Nov 6, in parliament:\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ has said the chance of the economy experiencing a double dip is small. But we feel there is a strong risk of a double dip." (Reporting by Rie Ishiguro)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/BOJ-QUOTES (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091217e5ch001ke\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
