\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Focus: Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears Fade Fast\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicholas Hastings   \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN   \par \uc2 844 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2009\par 09:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--What a difference two weeks can make.\par \par \uc2 Late in November, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alert, poised to reverse what appeared to be a relentless rise in the yen against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Fears were that, as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose--with the dollar falling to a 14-year low of Y84.83--it would pose a risk to Japan's already fragile recovery.\par \par \uc2 See chart at\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/3176"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/3176}}}\par \par \uc2 Now, all the pressure on the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  is off. The yen is sliding back of its own accord and speculation about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has faded.\par \par \uc2 In fact, some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialists, such as those at \uc2 UBS\uc2 , reckon the yen should now continue to weaken.\par \par \uc2 "We are buyers of dollar/yen over the next year," the bank's Gareth Berry told clients this week.\par \par \uc2 So what has changed for the yen?\par \par \uc2 Probably two things--a decline in the yen's safe-haven role as well as rising concern in the international investment community about Japan's inability to stage a sustainable recovery.\par \par \uc2 For many months now, the investment community has ignored the latter and seen the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a place to hide in a tumultuous world.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, however, talk of a global economic recovery has increased and, despite lingering concerns over sovereign default, investors have gradually become more adventurous.\par \par \uc2 News on Monday that Abu Dhabi is essentially bailing out Dubai--ensuring that the debt repayments of Dubai World are met--means sentiment in financial markets may well reverse, taking risk appetite back to levels seen before Dubai declared that it would not honor its debt obligations on Nov. 25.\par \par \uc2 This means the yen has become that much less attractive as investors prepare to take on more risk.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, recognition by the Bank of Japan that the Japanese economy is not about to rebound has added to the yen's woes.\par \par \uc2 UBS\uc2 's Berry pointed to the decline in short-term Japanese yields that took place after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bowed to government pressure and offered to lend another Y10 trillion at 0.1%.\par \par \uc2 This liquidity injection in Japan coincided with a rise in optimism over the U.S. economy when November's non-farm payrolls came in much better than expected. This helped to push short-term U.S yields higher, widening the spread with those in Japan and ensuring that support for the yen was undermined even further.\par \par \uc2 For the moment, this trend is only likely to continue.\par \par \uc2 Economic data from Japan has continued to deteriorate, with the latest Bank of Japan Tankan survey showing a worrying decline in capital expenditure plans that suggests business confidence in the recovery is shot.\par \par \uc2 With deflation now becoming entrenched in the economy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may well be forced to adopt further monetary measures to help stimulate the economy, especially given that the country's high deficit means there is little the government can do on the fiscal side.\par \par \uc2 By contrast, economic data in the U.S., including recent retail sales and consumer confidence figures, continue to surprise on the upside, suggesting the U.S. Federal Reserve could well start to exit its ultra-liquid credit crunch policies sooner than the market anticipates.\par \par \uc2 If the Fed makes any such signal after its next policy meeting later this week, this will push U.S. yields that much higher and ensure that the dollar's rebound against the yen proves that much more sustainable.\par \par \uc2 Early Tuesday in Europe, the yen was mostly lower, even though there were signs of haven demand as investors continued to worry about the risks of sovereign default. Hardly convincing Greek plans for reducing its budget deficit, as well as news of a widely anticipated downgrade in Mexico's credit rating by \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2 , both kept market sentiment in negative mode, with Asian stock markets mostly lower.\par \par \uc2 By 0745 GMT, the dollar had risen to Y89.01 from Y88.61 late Monday in New York, according to EBS. The euro was down at $1.4630 from $1.4651 but rose to Y130.24 from Y129.82. .\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg TNI FRX POV\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Reuters   USD/DJ \par    Thomson   P/1066 or P/1074 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Nick Hastings has covered the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets and industry for over 20 years. Apart from his written commentary and analysis, he also appears on Fox Business News and CNBC television in Europe, Asia and the U.S. He can be contacted on +44-20-7842-9493 or by email: nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkBackEurope@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 15-12-09 0815GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1066   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091215e5cf000kv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
