\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Mixed; Sentiment Uncertain Ahead Of Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicholas Hastings   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 633 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2009\par 11:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The dollar is mixed and the euro is weaker in Europe Friday as the market waits for the latest U.S. non-farm payrolls.\par \par \uc2 Although payrolls are expected to have declined less last month than they did the previous month, it is possible the data still won't allay concerns about the U.S. recovery.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, China's reminder that it will diversify its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves into other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is undermining support for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator said that while the dollar will still be the main anchor for reserves, there will be diversification among other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and high-quality assets.\par \par \uc2 The euro started the day higher but soon went into reverse despite a clear signal from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday that it is now winding down the emergency funding \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  it introduced because of the credit crunch. Although this move was seen by some as a start of the bank's exit strategy, others felt that the ECB is still cautious and failing to be as hawkish as expected.\par \par \uc2 Another major factor influencing market sentiment is the continued speculation over what the Japanese authorities might do to stop the yen's recent rise.\par \par \uc2 Japan's National Strategy Minister Naoto Kan kept the whole issue very much alive when he said: "Markets are reacting well to the government's recent policy action. But I hope the yen will weaken a little bit further."\par \par \uc2 See a chart of the yen's rise against the dollar:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/3138"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/3138 }}}\par \par \uc2 While direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains an option for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such a move is unlikely to get support from either the U.S. or the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 A report that \uc2 Dubai World\uc2 's creditors are rejecting restructuring terms has added to market uncertainty even though global sentiment had started to improve again during Asian trading, lifting the Nikkei 0.5% and the Shanghai Composite Index 1.6%.\par \par \uc2 However, the main market mover is still likely to be the payrolls number, which is forecast to show a fall of 125,000 in November, less than the 190,000 decline reported in October.\par \par \uc2 The market impact of a good number could be muted, though, given that other recent U.S. data has been relatively disappointing. Also, analysts pointed to the unusual warning from the White House that unemployment "might tick upward."\par \par \uc2 "We believe that if the unemployment rate continues to rise following last month's surprise rise, markets will react negatively and boost the dollar even if the payrolls decline slows to 100K," said Michael Hart, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with \uc2 Citigroup Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 By 1030 GMT, the dollar was hardly changed at Y88.23 from Y88.22 late on Thursday in New York, according to EBS.\par \par \uc2 The euro was down at $1.5066 from $1.5075 and flat at Y132.96.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was also hardly changed at CHF1.0000 from CHF0.9999 while the pound was up at $1.6623 from $1.6561 despite reports that the U.K. Treasury won't outline measures for cutting the budget deficit in next week's pre-budget report, contrary to expectations.\par \par \uc2 -By Nicholas Hastings, Dow Jones Newswires; 44 20 7842 9493; nick.hastings@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkBackEurope@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 04-12-09 1030GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1035 28038 4163 44462   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091204e5c4000s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
