\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 777 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2009\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN'S DEPUTY PRIME MINISTER CALLS FOR WEAKER YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's deputy prime minister said Friday he wants the yen to weaken "a bit more", a highly unusual comment that underscores how concerned policymakers are about a potential rebound in the domestic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA REGULATOR: NO CHANGE TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES MANAGEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator said Friday the country hasn't made any major changes to its strategy for managing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, in the face of calls from some officials and economists for greater diversification amid a weakening U.S. dollar. (published 0606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FRESH STIMULUS IN JAPAN WORTH AROUND Y24 TRILLION IN EFFECTS -KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's fresh economic stimulus package for the current fiscal year will likely have an effect worth around Y24.3 trillion, Kyodo News reported Friday, citing government sources. (published 0325 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: STRONGER-THAN-EXPECTED KOREA GDP PROMPTS RATE DEBATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's economy grew at a faster pace than initially thought in the third quarter, data issued Friday showed, rekindling debate on when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should raise rates. (published 0335 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: PHILIPPINES NOVEMBER INFLATION RISES TO 6-MONTH HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines in November accelerated at its fastest pace in six months but isn't likely to prod the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into tightening monetary policy promptly. (published 0416 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN BANKS TO RAISE RATES MORE THAN RBA MOVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two of Australia's biggest lenders said Friday they will raise their mortgage lending rates by more than the increase in official rates announced by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , risking further condemnation from lawmakers as they look to offset higher funding costs and protect margins. (published 0541 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA PM ADVISER: EASY POLICY MAY HAVE TO BE WITHDRAWN SLOWLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India may have to withdraw its accommodative monetary policy slowly, a top policy adviser to the government said Friday. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA GOVERNMENT: TO INITIATE REFORMS TO SHRINK FISCAL GAP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's federal government will initiate reforms to shrink a yawning fiscal deficit and bring it under control, the Finance Ministry has said. (published 0449 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOK MAY HAVE BOUGHT DOLLARS AROUND KRW1,152 - TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday to cap the won's rise, some traders said. (published 0547 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NEW ZEALAND GOVERNMENT ACCOUNTS WORSE THAN FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand government had an operating deficit worse than forecast in the four months ended October due to lower tax revenue that it indicated might continue into fiscal 2011. (published 0122 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBI CHAKRABARTY: NEED TO SEE HOW SUSTAINABLE CURRENT ECONOMIC GROWTH IS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will study the fiscal second quarter growth numbers to see how sustainable it is, a deputy governor said Friday. (published 0558 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM CONSIDERS STOPPING LOANS FOR IMPORTS OF SOME GOODS IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's Deputy Minister of Industry and Trade, Bui Xuan Khu, said Friday the ministry is considering asking banks to stop financing the imports of "unnecessary goods" in December to curb the widening trade deficit. (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR SLIPS VS YEN ON EXPORTER SELLING; BIAS UPWARD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar slipped against the yen in Asia on Friday due to regular Japanese exporter selling ahead of the weekend to settle accounts amid thin trade ahead of the U.S. non-farm payrolls data due later in the global day. (published 0540 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: WHAT IF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WERE TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ON THE YEN? \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With all the "will they, won't they" talk of late about whether Japanese authorities will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell the yen, it's worth considering whether any market action would have long-lasting impact. (published 0406 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: DOLLAR/YEN OPTIONS MAY FALL ON US JOBS DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options could edge down early next week if a key U.S. employment report shows that fewer jobs were lost in November, prompting players to further trim their dollar downside hedges. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(12/4) HEARD ON THE STREET: THE OTHER STEEPENING CURVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For government-bond traders, this year has been all about the steep yield curve, which has provided booming profits. (published 0023 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(12/4) GREENSPAN HAUNTS ROOM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Looking back, all the signs were so blatantly clear. And yet . . . the Fed . . . failed terribly in giving us the kind of warnings that we should have," said the silver-haired committee chairman, Chris Dodd, alternating between lavish praise for Mr. Bernanke and stiff criticism of the institution he leads. (published 0058 GMT) [ 04-12-09 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091204e5c4000es\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
