\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Down Vs Euro, But Pares Loss On ECB Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bradley Davis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2009\par 17:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar remained down against the euro Thursday, but recovered from near 16-month lows, after the head of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent a mixed message to markets.\par \par \uc2 ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet indicated an economic recovery is at hand, while the shift in procedures announced by Trichet amount to an incipient exit strategy from the ECB's unconventional policy measures to combat the credit crisis.\par \par \uc2 The ECB kept benchmark interest rates unchanged as expected and announced small steps toward withdrawing some of the massive liquidity that has been pumped into the system in the wake of the world financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 "The euro's reaction has been unenthusiastic," said Vassili Serebriakov, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Wells Fargo Bank.\par \par \uc2 "Still, as markets have now entered back into the 'risk on' mode, the dollar remains on the defensive overall," said Serebriakov.\par \par \uc2 In late morning trading, the euro was at $1.5081 from $1.5045 late Wednesday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y88.22 from Y87.40, while the euro was at Y133.02 from Y131.48. The U.K. pound was at $1.6585 from $1.6638. The dollar was at CHF0.9994 from CHF1.0017.\par \par \uc2 The Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of six \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 74.689 from 74.635.\par \par \uc2 There is a reluctance by the ECB "to put their foot on the brake aggressively in any sort of fashion," said Alan Ruskin, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy for RBS Global Banking and Markets in Greenwich, Conn.\par \par \uc2 The euro traded in extremely choppy waters during Trichet's comments at the press conference following the ECB rate-setting announcement. Erratic trading after major policy announcements is not unusual.\par \par \uc2 Trichet's remarks were essentially on the soft side, Ruskin said, indicating the ECB was in no rush to change the monetary policy that provides low interest rates and massive liquidity to banks that struggled from tight credit conditions.\par \par \uc2 According to Serebriakov, the details from Trichet were probably close to market expectations and there were few signals that the ECB's main policy rate is to be raised any time soon.\par \par \uc2 "The overall economic context doesn't suggest that they would want to tighten any time soon," Ruskin said. "There is a feeling that, yes, things have improved, but that nonetheless, the outlook is still quite fragile."\par \par \uc2 Still, the euro should remain on an upward trajectory against the dollar, Ruskin said, despite Trichet's comments supporting a "strong dollar."\par \par \uc2 The euro hit a 16-month high against the dollar last week, and traded near that level early in the New York session.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar continued its rise against the yen, as investors cast cautious eyes toward the Bank of Japan, which market players have been worried could be instructed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to temper yen strength\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision Tuesday to extend a new funding facility, which helps to lower yen interest rates, continued to drag on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Takashi Matsui, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Moreover, rate checks by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , considered to be a form of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the yen's surge to a 14-year high last Friday, are "still keeping investors cautious on the yen, Matsui said.\par \par \uc2 Emphasizing the challenge the global economic recovery faces in gaining traction, the Institute for Supply Management's non-manufacturing index unexpectedly fell Thursday to 48.7 in November, from 50.6 in October. A number below 50 indicates contraction.\par \par \uc2 However, risk sentiment got some support from the release of better-than-expected U.S. weekly jobless claims, which declined the last week in November. Initial claims for jobless benefits fell by 5,000 to 457,000 in the week ended Nov. 28, the Labor Department said, representing the lowest figure for claims since Sept. 6, 2008, and the fifth week in a row now that initial claims have fallen. Economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires expected an increase of 19,000 initial claims.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Canada Morning \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar gained against the Canadian dollar as crude oil dropped sharply and U.S. stocks opened lower.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was at C$1.0556 from C$1.0506 late Wednesday, according to EBS via CQG.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2654; bradley.davis@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Andrew Monahan in Tokyo contributed to this article.) [ 12-03-09 1118ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020091203e5c3000bw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
