\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 :Dollar Sharply Lower Against Euro On Recovery Hopes\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bradley Davis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2009\par 14:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar was sharply lower against the euro Thursday, trading near its 16-month low against the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as overnight developments encouraged investors that economic recovery was taking hold.\par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement of no changes to its key interest rates, which was expected, didn't have much of an effect on major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Investors will be listening during the 8:30 a.m. ECB press conference for any indications of when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might begin withdrawing the massive amounts of liquidity pumped into the system.\par \par \uc2 In early morning trading, the euro was at $1.5119 from $1.5045 late Wednesday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y87.91 from Y87.40, while the euro was at Y132.92 from Y131.48. The U.K. pound was at $1.6627 from $1.6638. The dollar was at CHF0.9976 from CHF1.0017.\par \par \uc2 The Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of six \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 74.442 from 74.635.\par \par \uc2 The late Wednesday announcement that \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  would repay its $45 billion Troubled Asset Relief Program loan helped boost the euro above $1.51, creeping close to the 16-month high of $1.5145, reached last week.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar rose against the yen as investors kept a cautious eye toward the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  for any signs of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter yen strength.\par \par \uc2 (Nicholas Hastings in London contributed to this article.)\par \par \uc2 -By Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2654;\par \par \uc2 bradley.davis@dowjones.com [ 12-03-09 0823ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020091203e5c30008t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
