\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar And Yen Fall; Euro Rises Ahead Of ECB\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicholas Hastings   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2009\par 11:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--\uc2 Bank of America\uc2 's plans to repay its $45 billion troubled asset-relief program loan helped to put the dollar back under pressure in Europe Thursday as general market sentiment improved.\par \par \uc2 However, the yen came under even heavier selling as speculation about official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop its advance increased.\par \par \uc2 The euro, meanwhile, was benefiting from expectations that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will give some outline of its strategy to exit its low credit crunch interest rate policy.\par \par \uc2 See the euro's advance against the yen in the chart:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/3127"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/3127}}}\par \par \uc2 Overall, the tone of global financial markets is cautiously positive.\par \par \uc2 Not only did the \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  news lift sentiment, but Australia reported a 0.3% rise in retail sales last month, contributing to hopes that the gradual recovery of the global economy is continuing.\par \par \uc2 The ECB is likely to provide even further optimism if it gives investors some hope that its emergency liquidity will soon start to be drained. Although the bank will probably confirm that interest rates themselves are unlikely to be raised anytime soon, it is expected to signal that the upcoming 12-month auction will be the last of the series introduced to help battle credit crunch conditions.\par \par \uc2 While the euro was being driven higher by these developments, the yen was being driven lower by increased speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Tokyo is looking more towards \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a means of halting the yen's advance.\par \par \uc2 Not only have senior officials held talks with the U.S. on the issue of the yen, but Prime Minister Yukio Hatoyama warned that the yen can't be left as it is.\par \par \uc2 While some analysts speculate that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets during the illiquid conditions over the New Year period, others suggest that any such move would sit uncomfortably with the Fed and the ECB, given G10 efforts to get China to release the yuan's peg against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "If the Japanese government remains concerned about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but wishes to avoid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one (option) is to push the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  towards debasement-style quantitative easing," said Gareth Berry, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with \uc2 UBS\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 The prospect of a weaker yen helped to lift Japanese stocks with the Nikkei ending the day 3.8% higher. Elsewhere, investor appetite for risk was more cautious with the Shanghai Composite Index losing 0.2%.\par \par \uc2 In Europe, most major bourses started off about 1.0% higher, helped by news that the latest composite purchasing managers' index came in as expected at 53.7 last month, up from 53.0 in October.\par \par \uc2 By 1030 GMT, the dollar had risen to Y87.78 from Y87.40 late Wednesday in New York, according to EBS.\par \par \uc2 The euro pushed ahead to $1.5119 from $1.5045 and to Y132.85 from Y131.48.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to CHF0.9976 from CHF1.0017 while the pound rose to $1.6665 from $1.6638.\par \par \uc2 -By Nicholas Hastings, Dow Jones Newswires; 44 20 7842 9493; nick.hastings@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkBackEurope@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 03-12-09 1029GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1035 28038 4163 44462   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091203e5c3000tm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
