\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Up Vs Yen As Mkt Looks To Japan Govt\b0\par\par\uc2 By Fabio Alves   \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 738 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2009\par 22:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar rallied versus the yen for a second straight session Wednesday as speculation mounted that Japan officials will take measures to arrest the recent appreciation of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A U.S. Treasury spokesman confirmed that Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat met with Treasury officials this week, a move that could signal \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be preparing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as it seeks to tame the yen.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is getting serious about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Kathy Lien, a director of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at GFT \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Late Wednesday afternoon in New York, the dollar was at Y87.40 from Y86.68 late Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG. The euro was at $1.5045 from $1.5086, as well as at Y131.48 from Y130.76. The dollar was at CHF1.0017 from CHF0.9994, while the U.K. pound was at $1.6638 from $1.6617.\par \par \uc2 The Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of six \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 74.635 from 74.426 Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities have stepped up rhetoric on the yen after the dollar plunged to a 14-year low, at 84.82 yen last week, in the wake of Dubai's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The greenback's gains began overnight after comments by Japanese Prime Minister Yukio Hatoyama, who was quoted by the Nikkei as saying the yen's sharp rise against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  "cannot be left as is," during a speech Wednesday in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 Japanese officials worry that a stronger yen will hurt exports, derailing an incipient economic recovery, as well as making it more difficult for the world's second biggest economy to emerge from deflation, or a persistent decline in consumer prices.\par \par \uc2 A Treasury spokesman confirmed that Rintaro Tamaki, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, met with Lael Brainard, the Obama administration's nominee for Treasury under secretary for international affairs, on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Administration officials declined to provide details on the discussions between the two, but it is likely the pair discussed the yen's recent surge against the dollar, market watchers said.\par \par \uc2 "The signals that we've heard from Japan have been somewhat stronger in the past 24 hours," said Vassili Serebriakov, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk is particularly high unless" the dollar trades consistently under 85 yen, he said. "The risk is that they will step up their response going forward, although it may not be necessarily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Speculation arose that the meeting between Tamaki and Brainard may be part of a process through which \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Some analysts reckon that the Japanese government could still attempt unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower.\par \par \uc2 "The Japanese authorities are ticking all the boxes to show they are doing all the things they need to do before they get involved in an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign," said Simon Derrick, who heads the Bank of New York-Mellon's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy team.\par \par \uc2 The dollar also rose against most of its major rivals, although the gain on the euro was modest.\par \par \uc2 Investors were in a waiting mode ahead of Friday's U.S. nonfarm payrolls data for November to gauge the pace of the economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 The market saw little reaction after the Federal Reserve said in its Beige Book that conditions across many of its 12 districts have "improved modestly." Consumer spending has risen and home sales picked up. But inflation remains tame, as the report said upward wage pressures were subdued.\par \par \uc2 Investors will also be eyeing the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision on its benchmark interest rate scheduled for Thursday, as well as comments by its president, Jean-Claude Trichet, following the rate-setting meeting.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the ECB to signal a definite intention to head for the exit," James Nixon, an ECB Watcher at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  in London, wrote in a note to clients. "Market stands to be surprised by the ECB's determination to reduce excess liquidity."\par \par \uc2 -By Fabio Alves, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2204;\par \par \uc2 fabio.alves@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Don Curren in Toronto, Brad Davis in New York and Meena Thiruvengadam in Washington contributed to this article.) [ 12-02-09 1648ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020091202e5c2000e9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
