\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Up Slightly In Constrained Trading\b0\par\par\uc2 By Don Curren   \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2009\par 15:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The dollar is modestly higher Wednesday morning as it shakes off earlier weakness against risk-oriented \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in cautious and constrained trading.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has strengthened against the yen as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffers from the reversal of earlier safe-haven flows and uncertainty about the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is pausing after recent gains in the euro and other risk-oriented \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and could remain in narrow ranges ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy meeting Thursday and the release of key U.S. nonfarm payrolls data for November on Friday, said analysts.\par \par \uc2 "The first thing to keep in mind is we are coming to the end of the year and the interest has dwindled a bit," Brian Dolan, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .com in Bedminster, N.J.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday morning, the dollar had risen to Y87.23 from Y86.68 late Tuesday in New York, according to EBS via CQG.\par \par \uc2 The euro is at $1.5071 from $1.5086 as well as at Y131.45 from Y130.76. The dollar was at CHF1.0001 from CHF0.9994, while the pound rose to $1.6655 from $1.6617.\par \par \uc2 The Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of six \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 74.435 from 74.426.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. private-sector employment report published Wednesday by payroll company \uc2 Automatic Data Processing Inc\uc2 . (ADP) and consultancy Macroeconomic Advisers showed the pace of layoffs eased further in November, with job losses dropping to 169,000 from a revised 195,000 decline in October. The market showed only a muted reaction to the data.\par \par \uc2 "I think it's a pause after [Tuesday's] risk appetite rally," said Matthew Strauss, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 . A sharp move higher by the euro ahead of the Friday jobs data is unlikely, he added.\par \par \uc2 "I would not be surprised to see a continued range trade until we get the employment numbers on Friday, which will probably also be the last significant data release ahead of year end," Strauss said.\par \par \uc2 RBC's Strauss said the euro will tend to encounter resistance in any move much higher than $1.5100. "We've managed to break above $1.5000 but it doesn't seem to want to go much higher than $1.51000," he said.\par \par \uc2 As a safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen was under pressure as risk appetite improved.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is suffering from continued market uncertainty over how Tokyo intends to tackle the problem of recent yen strength.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan announced an increase in liquidity Tuesday that helped to undermine support for the yen. In addition, some analysts reckon that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could still attempt unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower.\par \par \uc2 The yen also came under pressure after Japan Prime Minister Yukio Hatoyama said its one-sided rise against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  "cannot be left as is."\par \par \uc2 A report from \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  said other officials later denied he was pushing for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The pound was a leading performer against the U.S. dollar as traders sold the euro and bought the U.K. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The pound's gains also reflects its propensity to trade in a more volatile manner than other major non-U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Canada Morning\par \par \uc2 The Canadian dollar is slightly lower in subdued range trading Wednesday morning. The U.S. dollar is trading at C$1.0474 from C$1.0466 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 A report from Scotia Capital said the U.S. dollar is trading in the middle of its recent range from C$1.0207 to C$1.0870.\par \par \uc2 The near-term drivers for the pair are mixed, Scotia said. Support comes in at Tuesday's low of C$1.0406, while resistance is weak until the 21-day moving average of C$1.0560, it said.\par \par \uc2 -By Don Curren, Dow Jones Newswires; 416-306-2020; don.curren@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Nick Hastings in London contributed to this article.) [ 12-02-09 0943ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020091202e5c20009p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
