\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 936 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2009\par 07:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW JAPAN STIMULUS PACKAGE LIKELY WORTH OVER Y7 TRILLION -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government's new economic stimulus package is likely to be worth over Y7 trillion, a government official said Wednesday, as ministers scramble to protect the country's still-weak economic recovery from the effects of deflation and a stronger yen. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: BOJ SUDA CAUTIOUS OVER POSSIBLE IMPACT OF YEN'S RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy board member warned Wednesday that the yen's recent rise could undermine the country's fragile economic recovery, and suggested monetary policy would remain extremely accommodative. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ INJECTS FUNDS INTO SHORT-TERM MONEY MARKET; 1ST IN A YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan injected Y1 trillion into short-term money markets Wednesday, a day after it announced a new loan program aimed at stimulating Japan's economy, and reiterated its intent to maintain accommodative financial conditions. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA WON'T GO TO ELECTION YET ON CARBON PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian government won't yet go to an early election after lawmakers blocked a plan to cap the country's greenhouse-gas emissions, acting Prime Minister Julia Gillard said Wednesday. (published 0421 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: S KOREA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES SURGE TO A RECORD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves surged for a ninth straight month in November to a record, and may widen further with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely stepping up purchases of the dollar to stem an increase in the value of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOK SUSPECTED OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENING\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET TO CAP WON'S RISE -TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea may have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Wednesday to cap the won's rise, some traders said. (published 0240 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA CUTS 2009 INFLATION FORECAST; CREDIT GROWTH LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's inflation rate this year may fall below previous \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forecasts to as low as 2.9%, Bank Indonesia Acting Governor Darmin Nasution said Wednesday. (published 0505 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA FINANCE MINISTER: 2009 DEFICIT LIKELY 2.3%, BELOW TARGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's state budget deficit is likely to reach 2.3% of gross domestic product this year, below the government's previous target, Finance Minister Sri Mulyani Indrawati told reporters Wednesday. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MALAYSIA MIN:WON'T NEED TO UP FISCAL SPENDING TO BOOST 2010 GDP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia won't need to increase its fiscal spending next year even if it expedites major infrastructure projects to spur economic growth, second finance minister Ahmad Husni Hanadzlah said Wednesday. (published 0240 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA: DOLLAR AT IDR9,500 GOOD FOR IMPORTERS, EXPORTERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian rupiah needs to be slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar than its current level in order to avoid hurting exporters, Bank Indonesia's top official said Wednesday, while reiterating that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't let the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthen too sharply. (published 0600 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES 2009 VEHICLE SALES MAY RISE 2.3% ON YEAR -INDUSTRY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine's annual vehicle sales will likely record its biggest increase since the 1997-1998 Asian financial crisis, and is expected to expand further next year as the economy improves, an industry group said Wednesday. (published 0434 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par =FOCUS: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  COULD SPARK RUSH OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 If \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buckles under the pressure to devalue the yen, it could be open season for a global round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0530 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par =WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR, EURO UP VS YEN ON HIGHER ASIAN STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar and euro ticked up against the yen in Asia Wednesday, as firmer Asian share markets encouraged investors to unload the yen, regarded as the least risky of the three \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0544 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: BANK INDONESIA LIKELY TO STAND PAT THURSDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia will likely keep its overnight policy rate unchanged at 6.50% when it meets Thursday as the country's main price gauge showed a benign reading in November, analysts said. (published 0233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: MALAYSIA OCT EXPORT CONTRACTION LIKELY MODERATED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's exports likely shrank less in October than a month earlier due to weak base numbers in the year-earlier month and a stabilization in global demand, economists said. (published 0016 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: THE TOP EIGHT THEMES FOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The former politician turned author Richard Lamm helps us see out a volatile year on a cautiously optimistic note. Optimistic because 2009 was at least better than 2008, but cautious because of what may lie ahead in 2010. (published 0328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: GOLD'S RALLY SET TO COVER MORE RECORD GROUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold took a brief breather courtesy of Dubai's debt crisis and overbought signals, but momentum is now back and the yellow metal looks set to extend its record run as its traditional correlations break down. (published 0146 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS:DLR/YEN OPTIONS DN; SPOT QUIET AHEAD OF US PAYROLLS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options fell in Tokyo on Wednesday as the greenback remained relatively stable within a tight range, decreasing demand for short-term hedges. (published 0313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =POINT OF VIEW: THINKING AHEAD AT THE FED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Charles Plosser marked himself as a bit different by working the name of hockey great Wayne Gretzky into the title of the monetary policy speech he delivered Tuesday in Rochester, N.Y. (published 2218 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(12/2) FED DEBATES NEW ROLE: BUBBLE FIGHTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Not so long ago, Federal Reserve officials were confident they knew what to do when they saw bubbles building in prices of stocks, houses or other assets: Nothing. (published 0052 GMT) [ 02-12-09 0604GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091202e5c2000cs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
