\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -U.S. dollar posts largest gain vs yen in six weeks\b0\par\par\uc2 777 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2009\par 01:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yen outlook dims, investors wary of further BOJ easing\par \par \uc2 * U.S. private sector shed 169,000 jobs in November\par \par \uc2 * Focus on ECB policy meeting, U.S. nonfarm payrolls (Updates dollar/yen percentage gain)\par \par \uc2 By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The dollar on Wednesday posted its best performance against the yen in six weeks, after Japan's prime minister said the yen's rise cannot be left "as it is," prompting speculation Japan may take additional quantitative easing measures.\par \par \uc2 In general, quantitative easing undermines a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value because it expands money supply to levels that could potentially lead to high inflation.\par \par \uc2 "The bias toward yen strength that was prevalent the last few weeks has turned, especially after the Bank of Japan announced those quantitative easing measures yesterday," said Ron Simpson, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Action Economics in Tampa, Florida.\par \par \uc2 "Any time you mention QE, that's bad for a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So I think the risk for dollar/yen going into the end of the year is definitely to the upside."\par \par \uc2 The dollar also gained against the euro as the Dow's <.DJI> drop rekindled demand for the greenback as a safe haven. Investors were particularly concerned about the outlook for the financial sector, particularly after Sanford Bernstein put out a less bullish research note on \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 . For details see [ID:nWEN7068]\par \par \uc2 Traders were also hesitant to push the euro higher before Thursday's European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy meeting, when the bank is expected to announce details of how and when it will remove excess liquidity from the system. For scenarios story, see [ID:nGEE5B12A1]\par \par \uc2 The market's focus, however, remained on the yen in the wake of remarks from Japanese Prime Minister Yukio Hatoyama.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Hatoyama said it was unclear if the yen's recent rise was temporary but it could not be left "as it is," the Nikkei business newspaper reported on its website.\par \par \uc2 Japan's Chief Cabinet Secretary Hirofumi Hirano later downplayed Hatoyama's remarks and said they were not a comment about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nGEE5B10H2] [ID:nTKU105721]\par \par \uc2 That, however, did not deter investors from selling the yen.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS ON ALERT FOR BOJ ACTION\par \par \uc2 In late afternoon trading, the dollar rose 0.9 percent to 87.43 yen <JPY=>, pulling further away from a 14-year low of 84.82 yen hit on electronic trading platform EBS last week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's gain was the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's largest since mid-October, according to Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 Traders said a break above 87.50 yen would trigger pre-placed buy orders and herald a stronger push higher for the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The BoJ measures unveiled on Tuesday to combat deflation and keep short-term rates down also prompted investors who had bet on a stronger yen to square positions.\par \par \uc2 There are "concerns about the risk of further quantitative measures from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  or even \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which were exacerbated by the (PM) comments overnight and by the (BoJ's) policy announcement yesterday," said Daniel Katzive, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  in New York. "That's made the market a little bit nervous."\par \par \uc2 The ICE Futures' dollar index <.DXY>, which measures the greenback against a basket of six other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was up 0.4 percent on the day at 74.636.\par \par \uc2 The euro rose 0.6 percent to 131.43 yen <EURJPY=>.\par \par \uc2 But against the dollar, the euro was down 0.3 percent <EUR=> at $1.5045.\par \par \uc2 Thursday's ECB meeting is crucial, analysts said, and some believe that, contrary to expectations, the bank may not give details about its exit strategy from quantitative easing. That could weigh on the euro.\par \par \uc2 "The recent turmoil in Dubai has served as a reminder that ample liquidity remains of the essence to prevent contagion effects," said \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, a report showed the U.S. economy shed 169,000 private-sector jobs in November. While that was fewer than the 195,000 lost in October, it was higher than an economists' forecast for a loss of 155,000. For more see [ID:nWEN7048].\par \par \uc2 Markets are now looking to Friday's release of the U.S. November non-farm payrolls report. Analysts have forecast fewer job losses of 130,000, down from 190,000 cuts in October. (Reporting by Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss; Editing by Jan Paschal) ((gertrude.chavez@thomsonreuters.com; +1-646-223-6322; Reuters Messaging: gertrude.chavez.reuters.com@reuters.net))\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 11)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|J|UKI|Z|CANT|AUF|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091202e5c20000f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
