\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,063 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2009\par 08:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ CAREFULLY WATCHING ECONOMIC IMPACT OF STRONG YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Monday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is carefully monitoring the economic impact of the stronger yen, indicating a readiness to cooperate with the government to avoid any stalling of Japan's nascent economic recovery. (published 0515 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUJII:NEVER SAID TO RULE OUT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOR TIME BEING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Hirohisa Fujii Monday denied saying that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets was unthinkable in the time being. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT GROWS, BUT STRONG YEN A RISK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese industrial production rose for the eighth-straight month in October on the back of the nation's gradual economic recovery, and looks set to grow further through December as manufacturers said they would continue to increase output. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UAE CTRL BANK TRIES TO CALM FEARS WITH FUNDS OFFER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The United Arab Emirates' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has moved to calm fears of a bank run when markets and banks open on Monday by announcing a new funding facility for local and international lenders. (published 2009 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DUBAI'S DEPT OF FINANCE TO ISSUE STATEMENT ON \f28 \uc2 \f2 DUBAI WORLD\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dubai's Department of Finance is expected to issue imminently a statement regarding \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dubai World\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a senior Dubai media executive said Monday. (published 0746 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA JULY-SEPTEMBER GDP UP; ANALYST TIPS JAN RATE HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's economy in the July-September period grew at its fastest pace in 18 months as a surge in manufacturing helped offset sluggish farm output and stirred talk that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may raise interest rates as early as in January. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBI GOKARN: TO REVIEW FULL-YEAR GDP FORECAST ON BETTER DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will review its economic growth forecast for this fiscal year to March 31, after economic expansion in July-September trumped analysts' expectations, a deputy governor at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Monday. (published 0730 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA WEN: STABLE YUAN GOOD FOR CHINA, EUROPEAN ECONOMIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao said Monday a stable yuan is good for both China and Europe, and criticized countries that have called for a stronger Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  while also erecting trade barriers. (published 0613 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN AUTO OUTPUT, EXPORTS FALL FOR 13TH STRAIGHT MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's automobile production and exports fell from a year earlier for the 13th consecutive month in October as shipments to major markets declined, highlighting the extent of an industrial downturn which even government incentives at home and abroad can't turn around. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN GOVT: JULY-SEPTEMBER GDP GAP AT -6.7% VS -7.5% APRIL-JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's gross domestic product gap for the third quarter stood at minus 6.7%, a slight improvement from a reading of minus 7.5% in the April-June period, Cabinet Office data showed Monday. (published 0545 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA OCTOBER INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 0.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's industrial production increased from a year earlier for a fourth straight month in October, but at a much slower pace compared with September, due mainly to fewer working days in the month. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA 4Q GDP LIKELY UP MORE THAN 10% ON YEAR - GOVT THINK TANK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's gross domestic product will likely rise more than 10% in the fourth quarter from a year earlier, the State Information Center, a government think tank, said in a report Monday. (published 0015 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA DECIDES AGAINST RMBS LIQUIDITY FACILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Treasurer Wayne Swan said Monday the government won't go ahead with a liquidity facility to support the residential mortgage backed securities market, saying a consultation process with the banking industry had drawn mixed reactions. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA'S MCKIBBIN SAYS GLOBAL POLICY EASING NEEDS TO BE UNWOUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global monetary policy is distorting the world economy and policy makers need to move swiftly to stamp on a bubble that is already emerging, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  board member \f28 \uc2 \f2 Warwick McKibbin\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOK MAY HAVE BOUGHT AROUND $300 MLN TO CAP WON RISE -TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea may have bought around $300 million Monday to cap the won's rise during domestic trading hours, two Seoul-based trader said. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK CONSUMER CONFIDENCE WEAKENED IN NOV \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. consumer confidence weakened in November for the first time since January as households counted the cost of the longest recession since records began in 1955. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK HOUSE PRICES RISE FOR FOURTH STRAIGHT MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. house prices rose for the fourth straight month in November as a low supply of suitable properties continues to push prices higher in some U.K. regions, a monthly survey showed Monday. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: EUROPE'S YUAN RHETORIC A COMFORT BLANKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Does anyone else have a mental picture of European policymakers huddling on a mountaintop in the Alps, gritting their teeth and singing about a few of their favorite things as they watch the euro's ascent? (published 0633 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: REMITTING SOME WORRIES TO ASIA FROM DUBAI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dubai has been the golden child of the Middle East in recent years, riding a real-estate boom which it turns out has been unsustainable. The debt-laden city state is now having to restructure conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dubai World\f28 \uc2 \f2  and has announced a six-month standstill on the group's debt as it struggles with about $60 billion in liabilities. (published 0119 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: HK RETAIL SALES LIKELY UP FOR 2ND MONTH IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's retail sales likely continued to pick up in October amid a declining unemployment rate and rising visitor numbers. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: DOLLAR/YEN OPTIONS FALL SLIGHTLY ON STABLE SPOT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options fell slightly in Asia on Monday as the underlying exchange rate remained firm, easing demand for protection against dollar weakness. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =CHARTING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR BULLISH VS AUSSIE, KIWI THIS WEEK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/JPY is likely to consolidate in wide-range choppy fashion this week after rebounding strongly from Friday's 14-year low of 84.81. The daily chart is mixed as the MACD indicator is bearish, but the slow stochastic measure has turned bullish at the oversold level, while a bullish-hammer candlestick pattern was completed Friday. (published 0158 GMT) [ 30-11-09 0753GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091130e5bu000ma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
