8 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Hirohisa Fujii Monday denied saying that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets was unthinkable in the time being. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA WEN: STABLE YUAN GOOD FOR CHINA, EUROPEAN ECONOMIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao said Monday a stable yuan is good for both China and Europe, and criticized countries that have called for a stronger Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  while also erecting trade barriers. (published 0613 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN AUTO OUTPUT, EXPORTS FALL FOR 13TH STRAIGHT MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's automobile production and exports fell from a year earlier for the 13th consecutive month in October as shipments to major markets declined, highlighting the extent of an industrial downturn which even government incentives at home and abroad can't turn around. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN GOVT: JULY-SEPTEMBER GDP GAP AT -6.7% VS -7.5% APRIL-JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's gross domestic product gap for the third quarter stood at minus 6.7%, a slight improvement from a reading of minus 7.5% in the April-June period, Cabinet Office data showed Monday. (published 0545 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: S KOREA OCTOBER INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 0.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's industrial production increased from a year earlier for a fourth straight month in October, but at a much slower pace compared with September, due mainly to fewer working days in the month. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA DECIDES AGAINST RMBS LIQUIDITY FACILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Treasurer Wayne Swan said Monday the government won't go ahead with a liquidity facility to support the residential mortgage backed securities market, saying a consultation process with the banking industry had drawn mixed reactions. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: RBA'S MCKIBBIN SAYS GLOBAL POLICY EASING NEEDS TO BE UNWOUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global monetary policy is distorting the world economy and policy makers need to move swiftly to stamp on a bubble that is already emerging, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  board member \f28 \uc2 \f2 Warwick McKibbin\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOK MAY HAVE BOUGHT AROUND $300 MLN TO CAP WON RISE -TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea may have bought around $300 million Monday to cap the won's rise during domestic trading hours, two Seoul-based trader said. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA: NOVEMBER ON-YEAR CPI LIKELY +2.5% TO +2.6% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's inflation rate in November likely slowed to between 2.5% and 2.6% on year, while the on-month rise slowed to 0.01%, Hartadi Sarwono, Bank Indonesia's deputy governor, told reporters Monday. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: VIETNAM NOVEMBER INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 13% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's industrial production in November rose 13% from a year earlier to VND64.411 trillion, according to preliminary data published Monday by the General Statistics Office. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NZ ADJUSTED OCT DWELLING CONSENTS UP; PRESSURE ON RBNZ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of residential building permits issued in New Zealand rose sharply in October from September, data released Monday showed, providing further evidence that the country's emergence from recession is gaining momentum. (published 0032 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA'S BERAU COAL TO BUY BACK $325 MILLION BONDS -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's PT Berau Coal will buy back its five-year global bonds worth $325 million over the next four weeks ahead of its takeover by PT Recapital Advisors, two people with knowledge of the matter said Monday. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: EUROPE'S YUAN RHETORIC A COMFORT BLANKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Does anyone else have a mental picture of European policymakers huddling on a mountaintop in the Alps, gritting their teeth and singing about a few of their favorite things as they watch the euro's ascent? (published 0633 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: REMITTING SOME WORRIES TO ASIA FROM DUBAI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amid the recent hysteria in global markets on the Dubai debt worries there is a question worth asking: What does this mean for remittances to Asian countries like the Philippines and India? (published 0119 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: HK RETAIL SALES LIKELY UP FOR 2ND MONTH IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's retail sales likely continued to pick up in October amid a declining unemployment rate and rising visitor numbers. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =CHARTING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR BULLISH VS AUSSIE, KIWI THIS WEEK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/JPY is likely to consolidate in wide-range choppy fashion this week after rebounding strongly from Friday's 14-year low of 84.81. The daily chart is mixed as the MACD indicator is bearish, but the slow stochastic measure has turned bullish at the oversold level, while a bullish-hammer candlestick pattern was completed Friday. (published 0158 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =UPDATE: SANDS CHINA SLUMPS ON DEBUT DUE TO VALUATION, DEBT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Casino operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sands China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . fell sharply on its debut Monday after raising US$2.5 billion in a Hong Kong initial public offering, due to investor concerns over an expensive valuation and the heavy debt the firm has taken on to expand its Macau \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0617 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: KT, MBK PARTNERS PREFERRED BIDDER FOR KUMHO RENT-A-CAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A consortium made up of South Korea's largest fixed-line operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 KT Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and private equity firm MBK Partners has been picked as the preferred bidder for Kumho Rent-A-Car Co., according to a regulatory filing Monday. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ZIJIN MINING HALTED ON ACQUISITION OF ANOTHER FIRM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Zijin Mining Group Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said it suspended trading of its shares in Shanghai for one day on Monday because it is in talks to acquire another company. (published 0328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RECAPITAL WINS BID TO BUY 90% STAKE IN ARMADIAN TRITUNGGAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesian investment firm PT Recapital Advisors said Monday that it signed an agreement to buy a majority stake in PT Berau Coal from the Risyad Salim family's investment firm PT Armadian Tritunggal, in a deal analysts said is one of the country's largest in terms of value in recent years. (published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =WSJ: CHINA'S GEELY NOT INTERESTED IN BIDDING FOR SAAB - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Zhejiang Geely Holding Group Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . remains focused on its bid for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ford Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Volvo car unit and would not go after another global brand at this point, according to a person close the Chinese auto maker. (published 0445 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: GREENSPARK BIDS A$431M FOR ENERGY DEVELOPMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Energy Developments Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has received a A$431 million takeover bid from Greenspark Power Holdings, which is jointly owned by entities advised by private equity group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pacific Equity Partners\f28 \uc2 \f2 , but its board indicated Monday that it may urge shareholders to reject the bid. (published 0239 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AWB IN TALKS TO SELL LANDMARK FINANCIAL, RESHAPE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian agribusiness \f28 \uc2 \f2 AWB Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is in advanced discussions over transactions that will have the effect of transforming its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0140 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: OZ MINERALS M&A FOCUS ON ADVANCED COPPER PROJECTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OZ Minerals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it will focus its hunt for acquisitions on advanced copper projects that have the potential to produce more than 50,000 metric tons of the red metal a year. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CALTEX SHARES UP 6.1% ON HOPE OF EXXONMOBIL DEAL APPROVAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Caltex Australia Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . rallied Monday on renewed hopes its A$300 million proposal to buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 ExxonMobil\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Australian filling stations will get a conditional nod from the competition regulator despite earlier objections. (published 0519 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: HARVEY NORMAN SEES COMPETITION IN ELECTRONICS, APPLIANCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Harvey Norman Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gerry Harvey\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday the group's margins are holding up in most categories but that its audio visual and appliances divisions are under pressure from increasing competition. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHARAT FORGE\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 ALSTOM\f28 \uc2 \f2  JV TO INVEST INR20B IN POWER GEAR PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A joint venture company between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharat Forge Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alstom Projects India Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to invest INR20 billion over the next two years setting up a nuclear power equipment manufacturing facility in the western Indian town of Mundhra, a source familiar with the matter said Monday. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: LARSEN FORMS JV WITH NUCLEAR POWER CORP OF INDIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Larsen & Toubro Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . --India's largest private sector engineering and construction company by sales--has entered into a joint venture with the Nuclear Power Corporation of India to manufacture nuclear forging and other power equipment in the western Indian town of Hazira, a company statement said Monday. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 SAMSUNG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO BEAT 2009 HANDSET SALES TARGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 30-11-09 0706GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that it is on track to surpass its 2009 handset sales target of 200 million units, partly helped by brisk sales of touchscreen hand-held devices, including some smartphones. (published 0628 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAMSUNG HEAVY GETS $1.1B ORDER TO BUILD CRUISE SHIP FOR UTOPIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Heavy Industries Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's second-largest shipbuilder by orders, said Monday it has signed an initial agreement to build a $1.1 billion cruiser for Utopia Residences Co., a U.S.-based cruise ship operator. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BANK NEGARA PROFIT UP ON HIGHER FEE, INTEREST INCOME \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's nine-month net profit more than doubled because of increased net interest income and fee-based income, a senior executive at the bank said Monday. (published 0602 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AIRPORTS OF THAILAND FY NET PROFIT PLUNGES 90% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Airports of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday its net profit in the last fiscal year plunged 90% mainly due to a sharp decline in passenger traffic amid the global economic slowdown and domestic political woes. (published 0647 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:ASIAN SHARES RISE AS DUBAI FEARS RECEDE;FINANCIALS UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian share markets were mostly higher Monday, led by a rebound in most financial stocks after Friday's sharp selloff, as investors were reassured by indications over the weekend that any contagion from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dubai World\f28 \uc2 \f2 's debt crisis will be limited. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =FOCUS: JAPAN TRIMS TERM CRUDE INTAKE; MORE CUTS AHEAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's refiners are cutting the volume of crude oil they buy under long-term contracts, something some analysts say could erode their bargaining power at a time when India and China are importing record and rising amounts of oil. (published 0258 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA MIN: TO INVEST INR1.63 TLN IN RENEWABLE ENERGY BY 2017 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India hopes to invest INR1.63 trillion during 2012-17 in additional power generation capacity from renewable resources, India's minister for renewable energy said Monday. (published 0645 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: EU SEEKS AMBITIOUS VERIFYING OF PLEDGED CO2 CUTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European Union will press for ambitious reporting and monitoring of nations' pledged cuts in their greenhouse gas emissions, a lead EU negotiator told Dow Jones Newswires this week. (published 0530 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =FOCUS: GOLD SELL-OFF SEEN AS 'BARGAIN-HUNTING' OPPORTUNITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday's initial tumble in gold prices, triggered by news of credit problems in Dubai, may become a buying opportunity, as the financial uncertainty may give investors another reason to move into gold. (published 0530 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: OZ MINERALS M&A FOCUS ON ADVANCED COPPER PROJECTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OZ Minerals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it will focus its hunt for acquisitions on advanced copper projects that have the potential to produce more than 50,000 metric tons of the red metal a year. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SYNFUELS CHINA, BLACKHAM TO PLAN COAL-TO-LIQUIDS PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Blackham Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it has struck an agreement with Synfuels China Co. Ltd. for the pair to investigate the construction of a coal-to-liquids facility in Western Australia state. (published 0107 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BAUXITE RESOURCES: AUSTRALIA FIRB APPROVES YANKUANG PLACEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bauxite Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday Australia's Foreign Investment Review Board has approved a deal that will see China's Yankuang Corp. subscribe for 19.7 million shares at 50 Australian cents a share. (published 0202 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AWB IN TALKS TO SELL LANDMARK FINANCIAL, RESHAPE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian agribusiness \f28 \uc2 \f2 AWB Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is in advanced discussions over transactions that will have the effect of transforming its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0140 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: TOCOM RUBBER FUTURES UP 3.3% ON BULLISH ANRPC DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Natural rubber futures on the Tokyo Commodity Exchange rose 3.3% Monday, erasing most of Friday's losses with support from fresh buying, a weaker yen and bullish data on lower supply from the Association of Natural Rubber Producing Countries. (published 0541 GMT) [ 30-11-09 0706GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091130