\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's Fujii: never said  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  impossible\b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2009\par 02:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (For more stories on the Japanese economy, click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2  * Govt mulls steps to counter yen rise in stimulus package\par \par \uc2  * MOF's Tamaki may discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Washington -NHK  (Recasts, adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 30 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister Hirohisa Fujii denied saying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was impossible.\par \par \uc2  "That's a lie. I never said such a thing," Fujii told reporters on Monday, referring a media report that he had said so the previous day.\par \par \uc2  Japan's Mainichi newspaper had quoted Fujii as telling reporters on Sunday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets "would not happen at this stage" and that now is a time to monitor markets.\par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading around 86.20 yen <JPY=> on Monday afternoon, up from a 14-year low of 84.82 yen hit on Friday. [FRX/]\par \par \uc2  The government is considering including measures how to deal with the recent surge in the yen in an economic stimulus package it plans to compile this week, weighing slightly on the yen.\par \par \uc2  Fujii raised the prospect of a Group of Seven joint statement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday to cool the yen's rally as the dollar tumbled to a 14-year low against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  But he declined to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying he was not in a position to use the word due to commitments with other G7 countries on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility.\par \par \uc2  Tokyo has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since March 2004, the end of a 15-month long yen-selling spree totalling 35 trillion yen to stop a rising yen from hurting an export-driven economy.\par \par \uc2  Analysts say the market would grow warier of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks if the dollar fell to 85.00 yen, 80.00 yen or its record low of 79.75 yen. [ID:nT353201]\par \par \uc2  Public broadcaster NHK said on Monday that Rintaro Tamaki, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (MOF) top bureaucrat in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , will discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues with U.S. Treasury officials this week.\par \par \uc2  Tamaki will attend a seminar hosted by the International Monetary Fund in Washington later on Monday.\par \par \uc2  "It is true that he will attend the IMF seminar on Monday evening, but we cannot say anything further," a MOF official told Reuters.  (Reporting by Hideyuki Sano and Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Michael Watson)  ((hideyuki.sano@thomsonreuters.com; +81 3 6441 1827; Reuters Messaging: hideyuki.sano.reuters.com@reuters.net))  ((If you have a query or comment on this story, send an email to news.feedback.asia@thomsonreuters.com)) \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/FUJII (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|UKI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091130e5bu00016\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
