\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For November 27\b0\par\par\uc2 1,499 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2009\par 08:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or commentstoasianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THREATENS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS YEN AT 14-YEAR HIGH \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister Friday escalated his warnings against a soaring yen, calling the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise to a fresh 14-year high "one-sided" and threatening to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the rapid ascent continues. (published 0531 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:JAPAN ECONOMY STRUGGLES; THREAT FROM YEN RISE LOOMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese consumer spending sputtered and deflation remained entrenched in Japan last month, underscoring weakness in the economy as Tokyo grapples with a surge in the yen to 14-year highs that could hinder support from its export industries. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA SELLS MAIDEN 50-YEAR BOND AMID SOLID DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China sold its first 50-year government bond Friday, a move that expands its domestic debt market and places the country in a small league of nations that have issued ultra-long sovereign debt. (published 0614 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: S KOREA CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS RISES IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's current-account surplus rose to a four-month high in October, driven by stronger exports and smaller service-account deficits as travelers spent less overseas. (published 0309 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:NZ GOODS TRADE DEFICIT CONTINUED TO NARROW IN OCT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's annual goods trade deficit narrowed in October to its lowest level in seven years, Statistics New Zealand said Friday. (published 2354 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM STATE-OWNED BANKS AGREE TO CAP DEPOSIT RATES AT 10.5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's state-owned banks agreed to cap their interest rate on deposits at 10.5%, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: THAI FINANCE MINISTER: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MAY NOT HIKE RATES NEXT WEEK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said Friday that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  is unlikely to raise the policy rate at its upcoming rate-setting meeting. (published 0450 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA OCTOBER INFRASTRUCTURE OUTPUT UP 3.5% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's infrastructure output growth slowed to 3.5% on year in October from 4.1% in September, the government said in a statement Friday. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA REDDY: EXITING STIMULUS STANCE HAS STARTED GLOBALLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some countries across the world have started exiting the easy policy stance that was needed to cushion the global economy form a deep financial crisis, the previous governor of India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0533 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA RBI: CAPITAL INFLOWS SHOULD BE EQUAL TO CURRENT ACCOUNT DEFICIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India Governor Duvvuri Subbarao said Friday that capital inflows into the country should be equivalent or slightly in excess to the country's current account deficit. (published 0615 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA VICE MINISTER: WATCHING FALLOUT OF DUBAI WOES - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Vice Minister of Strategy and Finance Hur Kyung-wook said Friday that the government will closely watch the impact of Dubai World's debt risk and how it could impact the international financial market, Yonhap Infomax reported. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ADB OFFICIAL: AUTHORITIES MUST ENSURE ASIAN RECOVERY REMAINS STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian economies appear to be on the mend, but it may be too soon to begin unwinding the stimulus measures that helped cushion the blow from the global financial crisis, a senior official at the Asian Development Bank said Friday. (published 0529 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NATIONAL HOUSING BANK AIMS TO RAISE UP TO INR5 BLN VIA BONDS - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's National Housing Bank aims to raise up to INR5 billion through an issue of bonds, a person familiar with the matter said Friday. (published 0530 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ABU DHABI WOULD NOT LET DUBAI GO BANKRUPT - ANALYSTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dubai's request for a debt moratorium for its Dubai World conglomerate worried markets Thursday, but the Gulf city state can count on Abu Dhabi, its deep-pocketed rich brother, to avoid default, analysts said. (published 0132 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: ASIA'S CENTRAL BANKS GROW UP ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  actions of Asia's central banks suggest prudence is the order of the day as officials look to manage the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market rather than fight it. (published 0116 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: EXTERNAL DEMAND MAY BE A BUGBEAR FOR ASIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia might find itself in a spot of bother in 2010 given the risk that external demand fails to kick in. (published 2340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DUBAI WOES HIT ASIAN BANK SHARES BUT EXPOSURE LIKELY SMALL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia's bank shares were falling Friday on concerns about Dubai World's delay of its debt payments, though apart from U.K.-listed HSBC Holdings PLC and Standard Chartered Bank, the exposure of the region's banks to the city-state's troubles seemed minimal. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =4TH UPDATE: AUSSIE FINANCIALS DISTANCE THEMSELVES FROM DUBAI WORLD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's big financial institutions distanced themselves from Dubai World on Friday, although \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  caused a few market rumbles by declining to verify or quantify any possible exposure it may have to the state-run conglomerate. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSSIE RETAILERS PREPARING FOR IPO BLITZ NEXT YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A handful of privately held Australian retailers, emboldened by what has been a surprisingly positive year for the sector given the circumstances, are preparing to conduct initial public offerings next year. (published 0656 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MIZUHO FG: NOT AWARE OF DUBAI WORLD DEBT RESCHEDULING REQUEST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Financial Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is not aware of any debt rescheduling request from Dubai World, which sought a six-month standstill on its debt repayments to creditors earlier in the week, a company spokeswoman said Friday. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: TOP FRONTIER BUYS 28% OF SAN MIGUEL FOR PHP64.28 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Top Frontier Investment Holdings Inc. said Friday it acquired a 28% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 San Miguel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the Philippines' largest food and beverage conglomerate which recently diversified into heavy industries, for around PHP64.28 billion . (published 0616 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S METCASH TO BID FOR MITRE 10 GROUP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wholesale distributor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Metcash Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has submitted a bid to potentially take over Australia's largest independently owned hardware chain, Mitre 10, within the next few years. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA REGULATOR TO REVIEW HUATAI SECURITIES IPO MONDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's securities regulator said it will review on Monday a planned initial public offering by Huatai Securities Co., a medium-sized brokerage based in Jiangsu province. (published 0534 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GUNNS: ACCC OKS PROPOSED ACQUISITION OF ITC TIMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian Competition and Consumer Commission Friday approved a revised proposed purchase of ITC Timber Pty. Ltd. by forestry company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gunns Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . from agribusiness \f28 \uc2 \f2 Elders Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0531 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MITSUBISHI MATERIALS\f28 \uc2 \f2 : TO MAKE MITSUBISHI CABLE WHOLLY OWNED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Materials Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will make its affiliate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Cable Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . a wholly owned subsidiary via a stock swap arrangement effective March 12, the two companies said Friday. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHAREHOLDERS OF 3 LG TELCOS ALL APPROVE MERGER PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shareholders of three telecommunications units under the \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Friday approved a plan to merge in a bid to improve their profitability and their ability to compete with larger rivals at home. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINATRUST FINANCIAL CFO: COMPANY EXTENDED LOANS TO DUBAI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinatrust Financial Holding Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . previously extended loans to Dubai, the company's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chief Financial Officer Miaochiu Hsu\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0312 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CATHAY FINANCIAL OFFICIAL: BANK LENT US$10M TO DUBAI WORLD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cathay United Bank lent US$10 million to Dubai World as part of a global syndicate, an investor relations official at the bank's parent, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cathay Financial Holding Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., said Friday. (published 0336 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE AIR: NO TALKS AT PRESENT ON INVESTMENT IN OTHER AIRLINES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore Airlines Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . isn't in talks at present on specific investments in other airlines, but it remains interested in opportunities in the China market, company spokesman Nicholas Ionides said Friday. (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF AYUDHYA\f28 \uc2 \f2  CEO TO STEP DOWN WHEN TERM ENDS THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Ayudhya PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 's President and Chief Executive Tan Kong Khoon will step down when his three-year term finishes at the end of 2009. (published 0645 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SHELL, PETROCHINA TO DEVELOP SHALE GAS IN SICHUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has started its first joint development project in shale gas, in a bid to find alternative resources for the cleaner-burning fuel to meet the nation's rising demand. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASIAN RUBBER FUTURES FALL AS IRCO LIFTS EXPORT CURBS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Natural rubber futures fell sharply Friday across all major bourses in Asia amid long liquidation and profit-taking following the International Rubber Consortium's decision to lift 11-month-old curbs on exports, said trade participants. (published 0334 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CENTENNIAL COAL EXPECTS STRONGER 2H ON EXPORTS, PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Centennial Coal Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chairman Kenneth Moss\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday the company expected a stronger second fiscal half profit because of exports from its Airly and Mandalong mines in New South Wales state. (published 2343 GMT) [ 27-11-09 0702GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091127e5br000dk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
