\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Still Rising On Dubai,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Worries\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicholas Hastings   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2009\par 14:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The dollar is still rising after midday in Europe Thursday, driven both by fear of a debt default by Dubai World as well as talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This was a reversal of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent sharp slide which took it down to a 14-year low against the yen during Asian trading as investors continued to worry about how long U.S. interest rates will have stay at low levels.\par \par \uc2 See the extent of the dollar's dive against the yen in the following chart:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/3096"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/3096}}}\par \par \uc2 The dollar has also been driven lower by reports that Russia is planning to diversify some of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves into the Canadian dollar.\par \par \uc2 However, there was a sharp shift in global sentiment as news broke that Dubai World, a holding company for the Dubai government, had shocked financial markets with a request for a delay in repayment on about $35 billion of its debt.\par \par \uc2 Fear that the move could constitute an actual default led to a swift move out of risky asset markets with the Nikkei Index closing 0.6% lower, the Shanghai Composite Index falling 3.6% and most European bourses nearly 2.0% down soon after midday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was also helped up against the yen by verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Although Vice Minister Yoshihiko Noda initially claimed that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't under consideration, Finance Minister Hirohisa Fujii said that appropriate action would be taken against "abnormal" moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fujii also pointed out that the yen's rise was due to dollar weakness and not to yen strength. Analysts said this implied that action by the U.S. is needed to turn the dollar around.\par \par \uc2 "There's little sense that the government is about to act with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Standard Bank in London.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  appeared to have run out of patience with the Swiss franc's rise against the dollar and is suspected of wading into the market early in the European day with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive it back down against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't confirm the move itself but \uc2 UBS\uc2  issued a note stating that the SNB surprised the market with its move.\par \par \uc2 With the Thanksgiving holiday in the U.S., turnover in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is expected to remain fairly low, with the dollar likely to trade in narrow ranges from here.\par \par \uc2 By 1340 GMT, the dollar had risen back up from Y86.29 to Y86.71 but was still down from Y87.33 late Wednesday in New York, according to EBS.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was also up at CHF1.0028, after falling as far as CHF0.9916 and being quoted late in New York at CHF0.9960.\par \par \uc2 The euro was down at $1.5068 from $1.5143 and at Y130.65 from Y132.25.\par \par \uc2 The pound was also down at $1.6539 from $1.6722, with investors worried about the exposure U.K. banks have to Dubai World.\par \par \uc2 -By Nicholas Hastings, Dow Jones Newswires; 44 20 7842 9493; nick.hastings@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkBackEurope@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 26-11-09 1343GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1035 28038 4163 44462   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091126e5bq0013v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
