\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 936 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2009\par 13:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MAJOR EUROPEAN BANKS SEEN EXPOSED TO \f28 \uc2 \f2 DUBAI WORLD\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A host of European banks could potentially lose money from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dubai World\f28 \uc2 \f2  after the state-owned entity asked creditors for a six-month standstill on debt repayments. (published 1139 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DECLINE IN EURO-ZONE LENDING STEEPENS IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lending to businesses and households in the euro zone fell again in October to a new record low, the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 1016 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =JAPAN FUJII SHOWS CONCERN AS YEN AT 14-YEAR HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister said Thursday that he is watching the yen's upward trend "very carefully," suggesting he is becoming more concerned about the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise after it hit a 14-year high against the dollar. (published 0537 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =JAPAN PM: RAPID \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOVES UNDESIRABLE; NEED TO AVOID DOUBLE DIP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Yukio Hatoyama said Thursday "it is not desirable for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to move rapidly," the Nikkei reported. (published 1019 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: GERMAN STATE DATA SHOW ANNUAL CPI ABOVE ZERO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer prices in four of Germany's largest federal states rose this month in year-on-year terms for the first time since the spring, according to data published Thursday. (published 0908 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: UK NOV RETAIL SALES VOLUME +13 VS OCT +8 - CBI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sales volume at U.K. retailers improved sharply in November to a two-year high, a survey by the Confederation of British Industry showed Thursday. (published 1100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =CHINA SETS RULES GOVERNING BANKS' INVESTMENT IN INSURERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's banking regulator issued trial rules governing banks' investments in insurers Thursday, with a focus on controlling potential risks arising from such cross-sector investments. (published 1135 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =ECB WEBER: COVERED BOND BUYS MAKE PROGRESS AS PLANNED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's covered bond purchases are "making progress as planned," a member of the ECB's governing council said Thursday. (published 1052 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =BOJ OPEN TO REUSING SPECIAL LENDING FACILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan may reuse a special lending facility due to expire at the end of March if corporate fundraising conditions deteriorate, minutes of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Oct. 30 policy board meeting showed Thursday. (published 0148 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =ITALY NOV BUSINESS CONFIDENCE RISES TO 14-MONTH HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italian business confidence rose in November to its highest level in more than a year as short-term expectations of output recovered and the outlook for current demand improved, figures showed Thursday. (published 1134 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK TSY ADVISER: NAMING HIGH-EARNING UK BANKERS WON'T HELP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 David Walker, the author of a new U.K. government commissioned report recommending tougher rules for banks, said Thursday that naming individual bankers earning very high salaries wouldn't help improve corporate governance in the sector. (published 0853 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOE BAILEY: BASE FOR BASING SIZE OF FSCS CONTRIBUTIONS ON RISK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There is a case for calculating individual banks' contributions to the U.K.'s Financial Services Compensation Scheme on the basis of their riskiness, a senior Bank of England official said Thursday. (published 0952 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: ITALY OCTOBER NON-EU TRADE SHOWS EUR117M SURPLUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italy posted a trade surplus with countries outside the European Union in October, as imports fell faster than exports, statistics office Istat said Thursday. (published 0915 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =DOLLAR STILL VULNERABLE AFTER SLIDE; YEN SOARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar has edged back up after Wednesday's drubbing, but analysts and investors say it is still vulnerable to further losses, particularly as the yen shoots higher. (published 1024 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DUBAI DEBT WORRIES, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TALK HELP DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fear of a debt default by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dubai World\f28 \uc2 \f2 , along with talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , helped to lift the dollar in Europe Thursday. (published 1029 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =HEARD ON THE STREET: JAPAN'S DEMOGRAPHICS CLAIM FASHION VICTIMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Parasites. Not quite the right association for purveyors of $1,000, buttery-soft leather handbags. (published 1007 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  HAS GOOD REASON NOT TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  YET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen's surge to a 14-year high Thursday has Japan worried, but the government is unlikely to join many of its Asian counterparts and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, at least just yet, because the strong yen doesn't pose a major threat to its economy. (published 1013 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: BUNDS TESTING 123.04/12 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: Maintains the recent strong bullish tone following the push into fresh near-term highs above 122.70. (published 0814 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: EUR/USD TARGETS 1.5164 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: Forced a strong upside break through 1.5000 and into fresh 2009 highs above 1.5064 Wednesday to complete a bull wedge pattern. (published 0753 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: YEN'S RISE STILL HAS MORE TO GO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen may be playing more than just catch-up with the dollar. (published 0815 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: DLR/YEN OPTIONS UP AS DLR FALLS, BUT LEVELS LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen options rose in Tokyo on Thursday due to increased demand for hedges as the underlying exchange rate fell close to a 14-year low. (published 0324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =GLOBAL YIELD:HONG KONG SNAPS UP TREASURYS TO DEFEND DOLLAR PEG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong, the world's seventh-largest holder of foreign reserves, has become one of the biggest buyers of Treasury securities outside the U.S. this year as local officials stepped up efforts to defend the 26-year-old \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg. (published 1855 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Eva Szalay, Dow Jones Newswires; 4420-7842-9449; eva.szalay@dowjones.com [ 26-11-09 1200GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091126e5bq00108\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
