\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar off 14-yr low vs yen; SNB seen  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2009\par 10:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar at 86.70 yen, off 14-yr low below 86.30 yen\par \par \uc2 * Dubai debt problems dent risk appetite, support dollar\par \par \uc2 * Traders cite SNB selling Swiss franc; SNB declines comment\par \par \uc2 * Japan Fujii: watching \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 , will respond to "abnormal" moves\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Tamawa Desai and Jamie McGeever\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Nov 26 (Reuters) - The dollar edged up from 14-year lows against the yen on Thursday as renewed risk aversion prompted investors to shed riskier assets, giving pause to broad dollar selling.\par \par \uc2 A 3.0 percent fall in European stocks and a 2.0 percent drop in U.S. futures encouraged traders to trim positions that involved selling dollars for other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and assets like commodities.\par \par \uc2 Market players also refrained from re-testing lows on the dollar as trade thinned for the U.S. Thanksgiving Day holiday.\par \par \uc2 But dollar-bearish sentiment remained intact on views U.S. interest rates would stay low for some time and on pressure for the dollar to weaken to correct the U.S.' imbalances.\par \par \uc2 By 1518 GMT the dollar index, a barometer of its performance against six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rose 0.6 percent on the day at 74.752, up from a 15-month low of 74.170 earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 Dubai's shock move on Wednesday to restructure its biggest corporate debtor, Dubai World, and delay repayment on some of the company's $59 billion of liabilities, dented risk appetite across asset markets on Thursday, to the dollar's benefit.\par \par \uc2 "While much of the moves are going to occur in rates and credit markets, it is also being reflected in stock markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Lauren Rosborough, senior strategist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 The euro extended losses in late European trade, falling 0.8 percent to hit a session low of $1.5018. It had risen more than 1 percent on Wednesday to a 15-month high of $1.5145 on EBS.#\par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also hit a 7-week low against the yen at 130.00 yen.\par \par \uc2 SNB ACTS, JAPAN CHATS\par \par \uc2 The dollar also fell to its lowest level against the Swiss franc since April 2008, but the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise was abruptly halted as the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen selling its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose back above 1.0000 francs, having earlier tumbled to just above 0.9900 francs on EBS.\par \par \uc2 Some market participants said the SNB bought up to $1 billion in early Europe hours. The SNB did not comment. More dollar/Swiss franc selling was seen later in the day.\par \par \uc2 "As well as the retest of the perceived \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of 1.50 franc in euro/Swiss franc, we would note Swiss franc's overnight rally took the trade-weighted index back through the level at which the SNB first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March," said Adam Cole, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "That is perhaps another reason to think the central back will act aggressively to prevent further strength."\par \par \uc2 In contrast, Japanese authorities refrained from acting on the yen's rise, saying they were watching the market cautiously. Japanese Finance Minister Hirohisa Fujii said Tokyo would respond to "abnormal" moves as needed.\par \par \uc2 The dollar shot through a previous low of 87.10 yen to fall to 86.29 yen on trading platform EBS, its weakest level since 1995. Traders said 85 yen was now in the market's sights.\par \par \uc2 But analysts said the yen's appreciation was more a result of a falling dollar and Japan would need cooperation from the United States and Europe if it wanted to buy dollars.\par \par \uc2 "Unless the United States takes the stance that a one-sided fall in the dollar is unfavourable, the dollar's fall will likely continue," said Mitsuru Sahara, chief manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives trading at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ.\par \par \uc2 "The possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  depends on the pace of the dollar's fall versus the yen and its impact on other markets such as Japanese stocks and bonds."\par \par \uc2 For a snap analysis on yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , see.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since March 2004.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Ron Askew and Andy Bruce) ((Reuters Messaging: jamie.mcgeever.reuters.com@reuters.net; +44 207 542 8510))\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 6)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091126e5bq0002h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
