\par\par \b \uc2 SNAP ANALYSIS-Yen hits 14-year high but no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  expected\b0\par\par\uc2 By Satomi Noguchi   \par \uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2009\par 08:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 26 (Reuters) - The yen climbed to a 14-year peak against the dollar on Thursday but the market does not believe Japanese authorities will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  anytime soon because the move reflects broad dollar weakness, not yen strength.\par \par \uc2 JAPANESE \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  UNLIKELY\par \par \uc2 Although the yen has risen on the crosses on Thursday, the market sees the appreciation as a result of the falling dollar and the prospect that U.S. interest rates will stay low for a while.\par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts think Japan would need cooperation from the United States and Europe if it wanted to step in to buy dollars. This seems unlikely, particularly as the Federal Reserve described the dollar's recent drop as "orderly". [ID:nN24313828]\par \par \uc2 Market participants say the United States has little incentive to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when Treasuries continue to draw global funds and it is pressing for global trade to be rebalanced -- something analysts say means the dollar has to weaken.\par \par \uc2 Japan's Deputy Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda also believes the moves reflect dollar weakness and told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nT371315]\par \par \uc2 Officials say they must act appropriately against "abnormal" moves but one-month dollar/yen implied volatility, a measure of expected fluctuations, has jumped. It is still below 16 percent, where it has been since April, which suggests market moves are not disorderly.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  AT SOME STAGE?\par \par \uc2 The government said this month that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has returned to deflation. With the Nikkei share average <.N225> underperforming other markets, some analysts say the odds are rising that Japan could alter its "benign neglect" of yen strength and launch policies to deal with the economy.\par \par \uc2 In trade-weighted terms, the yen has risen much more modestly, as this graphic shows: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/zus63g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/zus63g}}}\par \par \uc2 Its real effective exchange rate -- a trade-weighted, inflation-adjusted measure of its broad value calculated once a month by the Bank of Japan -- was 117.8 in October, roughly 9 percent below an eight-year high of 128.9 hit in January. <JPYEEXR=J>\par \par \uc2 But the yen has started to gain on the Australian and New Zealand dollars, making traders more circumspect about the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  further down the line.\par \par \uc2 WHAT WOULD TRIGGER \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Speed. If the dollar's fall accelerates against the yen and implied volatility rises above 20 percent -- which would signal a disorderly move -- market players would begin to see a serious chance of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the market would grow warier of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk if the dollar falls to 85.00 yen, 80.00 yen or its record low of 79.75 yen. But speculators tend to use round figures as targets at which to take profits, which tends to slow the rise. (Editing by Jan Dahinten) ((satomi.noguchi@thomsonreuters.com; +81-3-6441-1875; Reuters Messaging; satomi.noguchi.reuters.com@reuters.net))\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /YEN (SNAP ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|J|SI|RBN|AUF|ND   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091126e5bq000ey\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
