\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar resumes broad slide, lows vs yen back in view\b0\par\par\uc2 834 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2009\par 08:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Dollar back under broad-based pressure, hits 14-month lows\par \par \uc2  * Yen gains as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  official says shouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * Rise in gold, commodities, stocks feeds pro-growth trades\par \par \uc2  By Charlotte Cooper\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 14 (Reuters) - The dollar tumbled to 14-month lows on Wednesday, hurt by persistent expectations for low U.S. interest rates, investor appetite for commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and expectations that Japan at least was not ready to break its fall.\par \par \uc2  It skidded to its lowest levels since August last year against the euro, the Australian dollar and a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but its steepest fall on the day came against the yen after a senior Japanese official signalled \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was undesirable.\par \par \uc2  Naoki Minezaki, one of Finance Minister Hirohisa Fujii's deputies, told Reuters that Japan should not step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market just because the yen rises, fuelling market suspicions that Tokyo is not close to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen gains. [ID:nT362093]\par \par \uc2  Already under pressure, the dollar fell below 89.00 yen towards a recent eight-month low at 88.01 yen, shedding 0.9 percent on the day and helping the yen rise across the board.\par \par \uc2  "In the beginning it was a general sell-off of the dollar. But in addition to that there were comments from a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official which reiterated the recent stance to accept the strength of the yen," said Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Japan at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2  Buoyant commodity prices, with gold rising to its latest record, and a rise in S&P futures <SPc1> added to investor appetite for pro-growth trades, with the Australian dollar gaining and the Canadian dollar nearing a 14-month high.\par \par \uc2  Dollar selling has rotated against European and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few weeks, with talk among traders that it, along with sterling, is being used to fund investment in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with prospects of higher interest rates and growth.\par \par \uc2  The dollar index <.DXY>, a measure of the greenback's performance against six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fell to 75.551, its lowest point since August 2008.\par \par \uc2  "The dollar should weaken and 75 on the index is a very important level," said \uc2 Robert Rennie\uc2 , chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "For the index to be there, the euro should test $1.50 and I guess the momentum is very much there for that to happen."\par \par \uc2  The euro gained 0.2 percent to $1.4891 <EUR=>, its highest since August last year. The Australian dollar rose 0.5 percent to $0.9145 <AUD=D4>, its latest 14-month peak.\par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve Vice Chairman Donald Kohn said on Tuesday the U.S. economy would not snap back quickly from its deep recession, fuelling market expectations for continued low U.S. rates which have kept pressure on the dollar. [ID:nN13198041].\par \par \uc2  Analysts said the next focus was economic data such as U.S. retail sales for September due at 1230 GMT as well as quarterly results from U.S. banks.\par \par \uc2  "People are interested in the strength of U.S. consumption. Consumption remains the source of problems for a U.S. recovery, and that would affect Fed exit policies," said Tomoko Fujii, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banc of America Securities-Merrill Lynch.\par \par \uc2  STAND-BACK STANCE\par \par \uc2   The dollar was down 0.8 percent on the day at 88.99 yen <JPY=>, heading back towards last week's eight-month low of 88.01 yen and towards January's 13-year low at 87.10 yen. It has shed about 9 percent against the yen since early August.\par \par \uc2  Minezaki said the yen's rise was due to dollar weakness and that weakness was likely to persist. Finance Minister Fujii has also indicated recently that the new government elected in August is likely to tolerate greater strength in the yen, although he and Minezaki have said rapid swings in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are undesirable.\par \par \uc2  Other Asian authorities are said to have bought dollars last week but \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2004, and analysts are sceptical it would do so unilaterally unless the dollar's fall really accelerated and it neared a record low close to 80 yen. [ID:nSP511068]\par \par \uc2  Traders said institutional investors such as life insurers had been selling dollar/yen and yen crosses, while hedge funds sold the dollar after it failed to hold above 90.00 yen.\par \par \uc2  The yen has not been as strong against the likes of the euro or the Australian dollar this year, although the euro fell 0.6 percent on Wednesday to 132.50 yen <EURJPY=R>.\par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar <AUDJPY=R>, which has been a favoured buy against the low yielding Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , shed 0.2 percent to 81.32 yen, although it was still holding close to its high for the year at 82.00 yen.  (Additional reporting by Anirban Nag in Sydney and Kaori  Kaneko and Satomi Noguchi in Tokyo; Editing by Chris Gallagher)    \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|GNN|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091014e5ae000cz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
