\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-New Japan govt faces tough short-term challenges\b0\par\par\uc2 By Linda Sieg \par \uc2 849 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2009\par 10:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Japan's three-week-old government faces a rising yen, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  looking to unwind some of its financial crisis funding measures and a fiscal time bomb -- all with the economy teetering between recession and modest growth.\par \par \uc2 Investors watching Japan must also factor in uncertainty over who decides what in Prime Minister Yukio Hatoyama's novice cabinet while eyeing an upper house election next year.\par \par \uc2 A loss by the Democratic Party-led ruling bloc in the poll would re-create the parliamentary deadlock that stymied policy under the past three short-lived administrations. Below are challenges the government faces and the policy risks that could result.\par \par \uc2 COALITION HEADACHES, POLICY GAPS\par \par \uc2 Despite a huge majority in parliament's powerful lower house, the Democrats must put up, for now, with two tiny partners whose backing is needed in the upper house to enact bills smoothly.\par \par \uc2 People's New Party chief Shizuka Kamei, a harsh critic of bare-knuckles capitalism, has already upset financial markets with a proposal for a loan moratorium to aid small firms, while gaps on security policies with the pacifist Social Democrats are another Achilles heel.\par \par \uc2 The partners' influence will be weakened if the Democrats win two upper house by-elections on Oct. 25, but Hatoyama will probably have to wait to see if his party wins a majority on its own in a mid-2010 poll for the chamber before dumping the duo.\par \par \uc2 STRONG YEN, BUT HOW STRONG?\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were jolted when Finance Minister Hirohisa Fujii appeared to contradict himself with comments that first appeared to favour a strong yen and then to backpedal by hinting at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after markets sent the yen soaring.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say, however, that Fujii has been consistent in saying that as a general principle \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should not be moved artificially, while his comments that a strong yen is "basically" good for Japan echoes the government's desire to wean Japan from export-dependence in the longer term.\par \par \uc2 Still, the new government appears reluctant to see the yen soar too quickly and endanger \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fragile, export-led recovery, so authorities could well \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves too far, too fast. Picking a level that would trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is tricky, though, because the speed of moves would probably be as, or more, important as absolute levels.\par \par \uc2 EXIT STRATEGY DELAY?\par \par \uc2 Market players must also ponder the possibility of government pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to delay phasing out emergency steps to support corporate funding.\par \par \uc2 Kamei this week engaged in blatant jawboning against the Bank of Japan (BOJ). While analysts say his heavy hand probably does not represent government policy, Fujii seems to have sent a similar if more subtle message.\par \par \uc2 Analysts generally expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to let some steps expire by the end of the year, and whether the BOJ would let itself be swayed by government pressure is an open question.\par \par \uc2 Government jawboning has been known to prompt the BOJ to act in the past just to demonstrate its independence.\par \par \uc2 FUNDING WOES, ECONOMY RISK\par \par \uc2 Experts worry the government will have to add to Japan's already huge public debt to finance programmes aimed at putting more money in the hands of consumers.\par \par \uc2 Cabinet ministers have so far identified about 2.5 trillion yen worth of projects that can be frozen or cancelled in an already-enacted 14 trillion yen extra budget for the year to March 31, so the funds can be used to help pay for new programmes worth 7.1 trillion yen in the next fiscal year.\par \par \uc2 But analysts say the government will probably need to issue more debt to cover falling tax revenues due to Japan's worst recession in 60 years, from which the economy is just now emerging, and may need to borrow as well to fund pet projects.\par \par \uc2 Hatoyama may also come under pressure to craft new steps to prevent the economy from slipping back.\par \par \uc2 The funding pinch could force Hatoyama to delay or even scrap some promised steps when the government drafts the budget for 2010/11, starting next April 1, disappointing voters. Analysts say a public backlash could be limited if he gives a convincing explanation.\par \par \uc2 POLITICAL FUNDING SCANDALS\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors have begun questioning people incorrectly listed as donors to Hatoyama in his funding reports, Japanese media say.\par \par \uc2 Hatoyama has admitted that an aide filed false reports, but said the funds came from his personal accounts.\par \par \uc2 Political analysts say the impact of the scandal depends largely on whether further damaging details emerge and whether prosecutors decide to press charges, both of which could at a minimum distract the government from urgent policy matters.\par \par \uc2 Hatoyama took over as party leader in May after predecessor Ichiro Ozawa resigned over another funding scandal. Fresh revelations in that affair could jolt the party since Ozawa retains hefty clout in his current position as secretary-general. (Editing by Nick Macfie)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-POLITICS/RISKS (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|RNA|ABX|BNX|FUN|SXNA \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091008e5a8000ij\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
