\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-BoJ seen unlikely to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2 ; yen tipped to weaken\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Cable \par \uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2009\par 14:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 7 (Reuters) - There is a fairly low probability the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the very near term because the yen will weaken against the dollar over the coming year, a Reuters poll showed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The monthly poll of over 60 analysts, taken this week, showed a stronger outlook for the yen <JPY=> than last month as the Democratic Party settles into government following its landslide electoral victory. However, median forecasts from 34 strategists gave just a 23 percent chance that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen -- although forecasts ranged from 5 to 100 percent.\par \par \uc2 "We don't expect ongoing yen strength to last for a long period, as being fully inconsistent with ongoing poor Japanese fundamentals ... We also see risks that the BoJ may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if dollar/yen breaks below this month's lows at 87," said Roberto Mialich at \uc2 UniCredit\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Under the previous long-ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) government, the country \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market earlier in the decade to stop a rising yen from harming exports, a key driver for the economy.\par \par \uc2 But that approach changed. Japan has not stepped in for more than five years, staying out even when the yen hit a 13-year high of 87.10 yen per dollar in January.\par \par \uc2 Yen policy under the new government is not expected to change, although analysts have said the longer-term stance is harder to gauge. [ID:nT87477]\par \par \uc2 Global economies have been thumped over recent quarters but economists say the corner may have been turned in the last quarter. [ECILT/WRAP]\par \par \uc2 Japan had been one of the hardest hit by the crisis due to its exposure to the collapse in world export markets and what was a very strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and there are some expectations that its recovery will be slower than other big economies.\par \par \uc2 "A return to stronger U.S. GDP growth next year should put the economy on track for fiscal consolidation. Along with the prospect of languishing output growth in Japan, this favours a rebound in dollar/yen above 100," said Kenneth Broux at \uc2 Lloyds TSB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Economists see the yen trading at 90 per dollar in a month, off the 88 it was trading at on Wednesday, before weakening further to 95 in six months and then to 99 in a year. That compares with September forecasts of 95, 98 and 101 respectively.\par \par \uc2 Yen volatility against the dollar was seen rising this month. Analysts say the divergence of forecasts in Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  polls offers a leading indicator of exchange rate volatility in the following month. [VOL/POLL]\par \par \uc2 SNB SEEN TETHERING FRANC The Swiss franc <CHF=> is not expected to move far from current levels if median forecasts, which are generally flat, prove to be correct.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  has made it clear it is willing to step in and stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise against the euro <EURCHF=> and this seems to be working with only a smattering seeing it breaking the 1.5 per euro level the market believes would be the SNB's trigger point for action.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro the Swiss franc <EURCHF=> was seen trading at 1.52 in a month, 1.54 in six months and 1.56 in 12 months, compared with around 1.51 earlier on Wednesday, hardly moved from last month's forecasts.\par \par \uc2 Median forecasts for the next 12 months see it trading between 1.03 and 1.08 per dollar <CHF=>, a slightly tighter band than forecast in September. (FOR POLL DATA CLICK ON <FOREXPOLL01>)\par \par \uc2 (FOR OTHER STORIES FROM THE POLL CLICK ON [ID:nL7544762]) (Polling by Bangalore Polling Unit; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -YEN/POLL|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|J|NAT|U|UKI \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091007e5a7000u8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
