\par\par \b \uc2 DJ MARKET TALK:BarCap Tips Crude In $70-$80/Bbl Band Over Next Mo\b0\par\par\uc2 1,273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2009\par 03:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0117 GMT [Dow Jones] Crude futures expected to trade in $70-$80/bbl range over next month or so, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "OPEC has already signaled comfort with that range, whilst concerns about the economic recovery are also gradually easing. There are encouraging signs in recent data flow showing Asian oil demand continuing to grow strongly year-on-year in June, whilst September appears to have been the strongest month for U.S. gasoline this year," house says. November Nymex crude down 71 cents at $70.11/bbl on Globex. (WMA)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0215 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Daiwa Institute of Research\uc2  says Nikkei seems to be hitting resistance around 10,100 neckline, making it important watchpoint. "A simulation indicates a bottom in the 25-day advance-decline ratio for the TSE 1st section (Topix), and an upleg is hard to imagine right now since special quotation fixing for stock index options/futures, which often diverts short-term trends, is slated for next Friday." Adds, concerns over yen appreciation continue to smolder; attributes run to new tax incentives in FY09 that prompted Japanese firms to begin repatriating funds from foreign subsidiaries. Notes, however, USD could stem its slide vs the yen around FY09 1H-end, while technical factors could provide further support, considering both 2-month and roughly 40-week cycles suggest JPY may be approaching short-term peak. "The proximity of the rate to the major low in January 2009 and recent fears of an oversold dollar could further serve to buttress the greenback, likely alleviating uncertainties in the equity market." (BMF)\par \par \uc2 0111 GMT [Dow Jones] STOCK CALL: \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  upgrades \uc2 Jiangxi Copper\uc2  (0358.HK) to Hold from Sell, raises target price to HK$16.50 from HK$9.50 after increasing FY09-11 earnings estimates by 16%, 194%, 35% respectively on higher copper price forecasts. Notes house's commodities team raised FY09-12 copper price estimates by 23.1%, 29.7%, 37.5%, 7.1% respectively on stronger-than-expected demand from China and tight global supply. Adds, 3Q09 SHFE copper price +19% on-quarter, implying strong sequential performance for company. But says views as fully valued despite tipping 2009-11 earnings CAGR at 26% as stock trading at 14.5X FY09 PER vs historical average of 13.4X and 2.11X FY09 PBR vs historical average of 1.94X. Shares closed Wednesday down 0.1% at HK$17.34. (LES)\par \par \uc2 0111 GMT [Dow Jones] Japan government likely won't step into market to curb a JPY rise if USD/JPY anywhere above 82, says \uc2 Daiwa Institute of Research\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Yuji Kameoka; "in the past, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the JPY became higher than the purchasing power parity. The current PPP is 85, so Japan would consider stepping into the market when the dollar nears Y80, say Y82." Adds recent G-20 statement, which says members will pledge to correct imbalances such as surplus and deficits, suggests U.S. may not be concerned much about a weak USD. Adds USD/JPY may fall to 85 in near term (last 89.53) as it's the appropriate rate based on U.S., Japan interest rate differentials.(TMO)\par \par \uc2 0110 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/HKD tad up to 7.7503 vs 7.7502, biased up on expected fall in local stocks, says trader at local bank. "The drop in U.S. stocks overnight could weigh on local equities and this correction could trigger slight outflows," trader says. Tips pair in 7.7501-7.7508 range near term. (YKS)\par \par \uc2 0109 GMT [Dow Jones] HKMA's new head Norman Chan says using U.S. dollar peg to maintain city's monetary stability and he seeks to further boost yuan business in HK in his 5-year term. "Chan's standpoint simply continues that of the former HKMA chief executive (Joseph Yam), which was widely expected and hardly moved the market," says senior trader at local bank.(YKS)\par \par \uc2 0057 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP tipped higher as USD gains ground against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; pair may move towards 47.30 after closing at 47.05, a 5-month low. Expected trading band 47.00-47.40. "We're seeing a lot of profit taking on short-dollar positions (vs other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). Disappointing (U.S. manufacturing) data again sparked some risk worries and sent the Dow down sharply," says local bank trader.(SFL)\par \par \uc2 0055 GMT [Dow Jones] LME copper lower in early Select trading, down $38 vs PM kerb at $5,942/ton. LME aluminum also lower, at $1,845, down $8. Mixed bag of U.S. economic data weighing on sentiment, China September trade data expected late next week or following week likely to drag copper lower, says ANZ senior commodity strategist Mark Pervan. September copper imports into China expected to fall below 200,000 ton level, down from 219,731 tons in August. "The catalyst downward will likely be China trade data for September. Copper imports will be slower due to seasonal factors, as well as coming off the exceptionally high levels from earlier in the year," says Pervan. Pullback in copper of 10%-15% possible. (EFB)\par \par \uc2 0047 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/SGD higher on risk aversion triggered by renewed worries about global economy, last at 1.4162 vs 1.4081 in Asia late yesterday. Trader with foreign bank says pair likely to continue tracking majors, but adds no sharp movements likely ahead of U.S. September employment report due later in global day; MAS semiannual policy statement later this month also looming, may also curb sharp movements for pair. Initial resistance at 1.4180, then 1.4230; support at 1.4140, then 1.4100.(VIN)\par \par \uc2 0045 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia government bonds may rise, with yields expected to fall by 2-3 bps, tracking gains in U.S. Treasurys, says dealer with local bank. "Bonds are likely to benefit from a shift to safe-haven assets following renewed doubts over the US economic recovery," says dealer. Still, expects flows to remain sluggish as investors unlikely to take heavy position ahead of weekend. Yesterday, yields on August 2012 MGS flat at 2.88%. February 2015 MGS down 1 bp at 3.73%, November 2019 MGS down 2 bps at 4.16%. (ECH)\par \par \uc2 0045 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY may hit 85 (last 89.50) by year end as global economic fundamentals remain JPY-positive, says Morgan Stanley Research. Adds that shouldn't be big issue for Japanese exporters as "JPY is not yet at a point where it poses a serious competitive challenge for Japanese producers"; says "indeed, USD/JPY would have to decline another 50% to roughly 50-55 levels to get to the same real level as when USD/JPY bottomed in 1994." JPY also attractive in terms of interest rates; "JPY interest rates are relatively high in real terms. When adjusted for core-CPI, they are among the highs of the region."(TMO)\par \par \uc2 0044 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD likely in 32.250-32.350 band with downward bias vs 32.319 last close; pair may return to recent weakening trend after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  just before close to lift pair up Thursday, says foreign bank trader. But notes stronger global USD, possible losses in Taiwan shares likely to limit any losses. Adds pair unlikely to fall below 32.000 short-term after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  yesterday, "foreign investors are deterred," she says. (WUM)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 01, 2009 21:17 ET (01:17 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020091002e5a200055\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
