\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -U.S. dollar drops to 7 1/2-month low vs yen\b0\par\par\uc2 691 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2009\par 09:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yen rallies, pushes through 90 yen per dollar\par \par \uc2 * Euro rises on strong U.S. consumer sentiment report\par \par \uc2 * Sterling takes a hit, falls to 4-mth low vs dollar (Updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar plunged to its lowest in more than seven months against the yen on Friday, weighed down by comments from Japanese Finance Minister Hirohisa Fujii, who said he opposed deliberately weakening the yen or any other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders cited a Kyodo News report saying Fujii told U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner in a meeting on Thursday evening he was opposed to manipulating the value of the yen. For details see [ID:nN25518058].\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the past to weaken the yen as this helped keep its competitive advantage in global trade. But the new finance minister believes that the yen should reflect Japan's economic conditions.\par \par \uc2 "People are now not afraid to sell dollar/yen below any critical level after Fujii's made those comments overnight since there is no longer any fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity," said Matt Kassel, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ING Capital Markets in New York.\par \par \uc2 Fujii was in Pittsburgh this week for a meeting of the Group of 20 developed and emerging market countries. A draft G20 statement leaked to the news media late on Thursday said global stimulus measures will stay in place, suggesting interest rates will remain low. [ID:nLH78576]\par \par \uc2 That also pressured the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because with near zero interest rates, investors would have less reason to hold dollar-denominated assets.\par \par \uc2 But it was Fujii's comments that traders talked about on Friday, practically giving them the license to sell the dollar against the yen as the greenback fell as low as 89.52 yen, the lowest since mid-February.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  THRESHOLD\par \par \uc2 "I think this year, dollar/yen can probably fall somewhere between 84-85 yen," Kassel said. However, he was not ruling out Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely, but he believed the government won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair drops below 78 yen.\par \par \uc2 The record low in 1995 was 79.70 yen, according to Reuters data. "I think you need to see a push below that to justify a disorderly type move that deviates from fundamentals," Kassel said.\par \par \uc2 In late afternoon trading, the dollar was last down 1.7 percent at 89.71 yen <JPY=>. The euro also fell 1.6 percent to 131.69 yen <EURJPY=>.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said investors repatriating funds before Japan's fiscal year hits the halfway mark on Sept. 30 also lifted the yen.\par \par \uc2 The euro edged higher against the greenback, helped by encouraging data showing U.S. consumer sentiment hit its highest level this month since January 2008. [ID:nN25501082].\par \par \uc2 The euro has been viewed as one of the proxy \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for risk appetite, moving in tandem with positive economic data and higher stocks.\par \par \uc2 The euro rose 0.2 percent to $1.4682 <EUR=>. A separate report showing U.S. new homes sales edged up in August also boosted the euro zone's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar fared better against sterling, which fell to multi-month lows a day after Bank of England Governor Mervyn King said a weak pound would help exports and the UK economy.\par \par \uc2 The pound <GBP=D4> fell to $1.5919, its lowest since early June, before edging back to $1.5931, down 0.8 percent, while the euro rose above 92 pence <EURGBP=> for the first time since April.\par \par \uc2 King's comments hit the UK \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as did perceptions that the Bank of England will lag other central banks in ending its loose monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Federal Reserve Governor Kevin Warsh said on Friday U.S. interest rates could rise sooner than most people expect, which helped ease the negative stance on the dollar. [ID:nN25513396]. (Additional reporting by Steven C. Johnson; Editing by Kenneth Barry)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 9)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|J|UKI|Z|CANT|AUF|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090925e59p000vb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
