\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: BOJ Gov Remarks On Strong Yen Effect Lift  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Megumi Fujikawa and Tomoyuki Tachikawa \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2009\par 11:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The yen got a lift Thursday from remarks by Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa suggesting he thinks a stronger domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may benefit the economy in the long term, though he also said such rises could depress prices in the near term and that stable movement in the market is desirable.\par \par \uc2 "If the yen becomes stronger, that could push prices down in the short term," Shirakawa said at a regular press conference. "But certainly, that may help boost the economy in the long run."\par \par \uc2 Coming a day after the start of the new Democratic Party of Japan government, whose finance minister said a strong yen could be good for the country by increasing consumers' purchasing power, the remarks caused a brief flurry of yen buying on speculation that the BOJ chief shares the new government's tolerance of a higher yen. Immediately after Shirakawa's remarks, the dollar dropped to around Y90.50 from Y90.90.\par \par \uc2 The yen has been strengthening in recent weeks, partly on worries about the U.S. economic outlook and the health of the U.S. financial sector. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen by more than six yen since the start of July, to a seven-month low of Y90.12 Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 However, Shirakawa's remarks were a reiteration of his previous views on the yen, and they appeared to move the market mainly because traders were jittery about the new administration's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. In any case, the BOJ isn't in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  - that is the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's job.\par \par \uc2 New Japanese Finance Minister Hirohisa Fujii said early Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should generally not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and that "the idea that the yen should be cheaper for the sake of (Japan's) exporters is wrong."\par \par \uc2 Asked whether Shirakawa agreed with Fujii's views, the BOJ chief didn't directly answer, but said: "Stable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves are desirable for the economy," he said. "We will keep an eye on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves down the road."\par \par \uc2 Shirakawa also showed a more relaxed attitude toward Japan's economic downside risks, saying they "seem to be diminishing compared with the period after the collapse of \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 " in Sep. 2008.\par \par \uc2 His comments came after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  revised up its economic assessment for the first time since July. It said "Japan's economic conditions are showing signs of recovery."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted its assessment of exports and production as well as corporate funding conditions. It also noted that there is a higher chance that emerging economies would recover quicker than expected.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ board also voted unanimously to keep its unsecured overnight call loan rate unchanged at 0.1% in September. The board last lowered the policy interest rate in December, by 20 basis points.\par \par \uc2 -By Megumi Fujikawa and Tomoyuki Tachikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com, 813-6895-7559; tomoyuki.tachikawa@dowjones.com, 813-6895-7556 [ 17-09-09 0949GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090917e59h000et\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
