\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 926 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2009\par 09:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =AUSTRALIAN LEADING ECONOMIC INDEX IMPROVES IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian economy continues to shows signs of a solid recovery with a leading index of economic activity Wednesday showing strong improvement in July. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S: MAY RAISE S KOREA SOVEREIGN RTGS IF ECONOMY IMPROVES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service may raise its sovereign ratings for South Korea if the country's economy continues to improve, but any upgrade is unlikely over the next 12 months, an executive at the ratings firm said Wednesday. (published 0502 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN LOWER HOUSE VOTES FOR DPJ HATOYAMA AS PRIME MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Lower House of Parliament Wednesday named Yukio Hatoyama as the country's new prime minister, a move that will result in the first change of government by a political party with a solid majority for over half a century. (published 0552 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S INCOMING FIN MIN: AGAINST \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Incoming Japanese Finance Minister Hirohisa Fujii said that the recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market "is not fluctuating wildly" and therefore does not call for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Nikkei and other media reported Wednesday. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA:TO ACT IF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MKT MOVEMENTS ARE "SHARPLY ONE-SIDED"-REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government plans to act "as needed" if movements in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market are "sharply one-sided", Yonhap Infomax reported Wednesday, citing the finance ministry. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA AUG SEASONALLY ADJUSTED JOBLESS 3.8% VS 3.8% JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's seasonally adjusted jobless rate was at 3.8% in August, the same as a month earlier, government data showed Wednesday. (published 0450 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HKMA SOLD HK$1.55 BLN TO DEFEND US DLR PEG TUESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it sold HK$1.55 billion in New York's Tuesday trading session to defend the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar. (published 0010 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =NATIONAL AUSTRALIA BANK TO ISSUE US$500M HYBRID BOND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 National Australia Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday it plans to issue US$500 million of hybrid tier 1 capital securities to offshore investors. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJE(9/16) UPDATE: IMF OUTLINES HOW TO END GOVT AID TO BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund, reinforcing its role in remaking the global economy, laid out detailed principles for scaling back government support of the financial industry over coming years. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =GEITHNER, REGULATORS TO TESTIFY ON FINCL MKT REGULATION REFORM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner and federal financial regulators will head to Capitol Hill in the coming weeks as lawmakers step up work on legislation to revamp regulation of the financial markets. (published 2202 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA TO EASE BUSINESS REGULATIONS TO BOOST DOMESTIC DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea plans to ease business regulations to help boost sagging domestic demand and attract more investment from abroad, the Ministry of Strategy and Economy said Wednesday. (published 0111 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =NZ GOVT TO PROCEED WITH NZ$1.5B BROADBAND PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand government said Wednesday it would proceed with a NZ$1.5 billion investment to build a national broadband network together with the private sector, while rejecting counterproposals by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telecom Corp. of New Zealand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and Vodafone New Zealand, a unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vodafone Group PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  . (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA MIN:TO SEEK CABINET OK TO INFUSE EQUITY IN AIR INDIA SOON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's aviation ministry will shortly seek the federal Cabinet's approval to infuse fresh equity capital in state-run carrier Air India, Civil Aviation Minister Praful Patel said Wednesday. (published 0608 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par =WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : EURO HITS 6TH STRAIGHT 9-MONTH HIGH VS DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro advanced to a new nine-month high against the dollar Tuesday for the sixth consecutive trading session. (published 2130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: USD/JPY CONTINUES ITS DESCENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following are forecasts for Wednesday's trading session. They may, at times, be at odds with the three-day and weekly trends in the table above. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: BUNDS, EURIBOR CAPPED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December bund and March euribor futures are considered to be capped now, following Tuesday's falls. Gilt futures may stay capped as well with only March short sterling futures continuing to make new all-time highs and remaining well bid. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: DLR/YEN OPTIONS DOWN,BUT MAY RISE INTO WEEKEND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options edged down in Tokyo Wednesday as some players looked to sell dollar downside hedges as the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared to be stable around Y91. (published 0403 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: HK JUN-AUG JOBLESS RATE LIKELY EDGED UP TO 5.5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's unemployment rate likely edged up in the three months ended Aug. 31, as firms remained cautious about hiring more staff while university graduates begun entering the job market, economists said. (published 0324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CREDIT MARKETS: IT'S AS THOUGH LEHMAN NEVER HAPPENED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit markets were buoyed further Tuesday after retail sales and manufacturing data boosted some hopes that the end of the recession could be near. (published 2021 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =HEARD ON THE STREET: THE UK'S FISCAL OVERSTRETCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gordon Brown has finally acknowledged the need for U.K. public spending cuts. The debate now is not just over the details of those cuts but their timing. (published 2052 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(9/16) BERNANKE SEES END TO US RECESSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke said Tuesday that the recession was "very likely over," as consumers showed some of the first tangible signs of spending again. (published 0037 GMT) [ 16-09-09 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090916e59g00088\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip