\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Senior DPJ Member: Party Would Refrain From  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 719 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2009\par 04:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 19 Aug 2009 22:24 EDT =DJ  INTERVIEW:Senior DPJ Member: To Refrain From \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Nakamichi \par    OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Democratic Party of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the yen fluctuates too sharply, a senior party lawmaker said, another indication that the DPJ will continue Japan's free-market approach toward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The comments from Tetsuro Fukuyama, an Upper-House member and deputy chair of the DPJ's Policy Research Committee, come amid growing expectations that the party will win an Aug. 30 general election and form its first-ever government.\par \par \uc2 "Political interference could have various effects on markets," Fukuyama said in a recent interview with Dow Jones Newswires. "I believe that a DPJ government, fundamentally, would be inclined to refrain from the use of political \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into market activity," including \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, he said.\par \par \uc2 Fukuyama indicated that excessive volatility in exchange rates would be necessary to spur the DPJ to action.\par \par \uc2 "Whether it's a rise or a decline in the yen, abrupt fluctuations (in exchange rates) could have a strong impact on economic fundamentals, so we must avoid that situation," he said.\par \par \uc2 Fukuyama's remarks are the latest indication that the DPJ would follow \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's five-year-old policy of refraining from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets except in extreme circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Over the last few weeks, other DPJ officials have signaled tolerance toward potential yen rises, seemingly more attuned to the benefits, rather than the drawbacks, of a strong domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While a strong yen would hurt Japan's exporters, holding the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down would risk keeping the nation's economy as reliant on external demand as ever, hindering the DPJ's bid to build domestic-demand-led growth. An appreciation in the yen could make foreign goods and raw materials cheaper for consumers and manufacturers.\par \par \uc2 The dollar stood at Y94.23 around 0100 GMT Thursday, down about 24% compared with levels seen in June 2007, but above the 13-year low of Y87.10 in January of this year.\par \par \uc2 Fukuyama also hinted that if the global financial turmoil seen after the collapse of U.S. investment bank \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  last September occurs again, a DPJ government might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets in cooperation with other countries.\par \par \uc2 "I wouldn't rule out the possibility that if advanced economies across the globe deteriorate sharply, just as they did after the Lehman shock, then the DPJ government would coordinate policy steps with other nations," he said.\par \par \uc2 Worth Creating A New MOF Post For International Finance\par \par \uc2 On the issue of administrative reform, Fukuyama voiced support for the idea of creating a quasi-ministerial post for international affairs at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The proposal comes from Hirohisa Fujii, a top adviser for the DPJ and former finance minister, who wants the party to assert more political leadership over international finance policy than the ruling Liberal Democratic Party.\par \par \uc2 Fujii has told Dow Jones that the proposed position should carry power equivalent to ministerial level in international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financial negotiations.\par \par \uc2 "It's an idea from Mr. Fujii, who has served as finance minister and has plenty of experience. There's no doubt that his idea is worth attentively listening to" within the party, Fukuyama said.\par \par \uc2 Fukuyama declined to comment on how quickly the party might establish the post after wining the election, but he said the DPJ must do something to improve Japan's ability to deal with global financial problems.\par \par \uc2 "To be honest, I don't think that even MOF officials are receiving sufficient training or have enough expertise in the area of international finance," he said.\par \par \uc2 "In Japan's public sector, there're just too few people who are able to handle issues about international financial markets. We ought to create the environment needed to increase the number of specialists capable of making policy decisions regarding international finance in Japan," he said.\par \par \uc2 At present, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies and other cross-border issues are largely handled by elite MOF bureaucrats, with the finance minister often preoccupied with domestic policy matters.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6895-7558; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 19, 2009 22:24 ET (02:24 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090820e58k000fo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
